ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,1,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The euro area bank lending survey Fourth quarter of 2023 January 2024
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,2,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Contents 1 Overview of results 3 Box 1 General notes 5 2 Loans to enterprises 6 2.1 Credit standards tightened moderately further 6 2.2 Terms and conditions tightened moderately further 9 2.3 Rejection rates increased 11 2.4 Net demand for loans continued to decrease markedly 12 3 Loans to households for house purchase 15 3.1 Credit standards tightened somewhat further 15 3.2 Terms and conditions eased somewhat 16 3.3 Rejection rates increased 18 3.4 Net demand for loans decreased strongly 19 4 Consumer credit and other lending to households 21 4.1 Credit standards tightened further 21 4.2 Terms and conditions tightened further 22 4.3 Rejection rates increased 24 4.4 Net demand for loans decreased moderately further 24 5 Ad hoc questions 26 5.1 Banks’ access to retail and wholesale funding improved 26 5.2 Banks increased their capital in response to regulatory and supervisory requirements 27 5.3 Perceived credit risks in banks’ loan portfolios had a tightening impact on credit standards 30 5.4 Bank lending conditions tightened further in most economic sectors 33 5.5 Decrease in excess liquidity had a limited impact 36 Annexes 38 2 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Overview of results
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"1 Overview of results In the January 2024 bank lending survey (BLS), euro area banks moderately tightened their credit standards further for loans or credit lines to enterprises in the fourth quarter of 2023 (net percentage of banks of 4%; see Overview table).1 The tightening adds to the substantial cumulative tightening since 2022, which has contributed, together with weak demand, to the strong fall in loan growth to firms."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks’ risk perceptions related to the economic outlook and the situation of firms continued to have a tightening impact, whereas the impact of banks’ cost of funds and balance sheet situations, competition and risk tolerance was broadly neutral at the euro area level in the fourth quarter of 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"While banks in three out of the four largest euro area countries saw unchanged credit standards, banks in most of these countries reported a perception of greater risks."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The impact of past tightening will continue to dampen loan growth in the coming quarters, in line with the leading indicator properties of credit standards (about 5-6 quarters ahead of actual loan growth developments), such that actual lending to firms can be expected to remain weak in 2024."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The net percentage of banks reporting a tightening moderated compared with the previous quarter (12% in the third quarter of 2023), was lower than banks had expected (7%) and lower than the historical average (9%)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"At the same time, banks expect further net tightening for the first quarter of 2024 (9%)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks reported a further net tightening of credit standards for loans to households in the fourth quarter of 2023, which was small for housing loans and more pronounced for consumer credit (net percentages of 2% and 11% respectively; see Overview table)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Risk perceptions were a major driver of the tightening of credit standards in both categories, with banks’ lower risk tolerance also driving the tightening of credit standards for consumer credit."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"While the slight tightening in the housing loan segment was driven by smaller euro area countries, credit standards in consumer credit tightened across the four largest euro area economies."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"For both loan categories, the net tightening was lower compared with the third quarter (11% for housing loans and 16% for consumer credit) but was broadly in line with what had been expected."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Banks expect a further net tightening of credit standards in both loan categories.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Firms’ net demand for loans continued to decrease markedly in the fourth quarter of 2023 (net percentage of -20%; see Overview table).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The decline in loan demand was mainly driven by higher interest rates, reported by banks in all four of the largest euro area economies, and lower fixed investment, consistent with the net decrease in demand for long-term loans."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"By contrast, financing needs for inventories and working capital contributed slightly positively to loan demand."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"While the net percentage of banks reporting a decrease was considerably smaller than its all-time low in the second quarter of 2023 (-42%), the renewed decline added to the substantial net 1 The results reported in the January 2024 bank lending survey (BLS) relate to changes observed during the fourth quarter of 2023 and expectations for the first quarter of 2024."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The survey was conducted between 8 December 2023 and 2 January 2024.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,16,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"A total of 157 banks were surveyed in this round, with a response rate of 100%."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,17,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In addition to results for the euro area as a whole, this report contains results for the four largest euro area countries in terms of GDP (i.e. Germany, France, Italy, Spain)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,3,18,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,3 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Overview of results
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,decreases in loan demand over the previous four quarters.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The decline in net demand was in line with banks’ expectations.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first quarter of 2024, banks expect a small net increase in demand for loans to firms for the first time since the second quarter of 2022."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Net demand for housing loans and consumer credit continued to decrease (net percentages of -26% and -7% respectively; see Overview table).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"For both housing loans and consumer credit, the general level of interest rates and consumer confidence were major drivers of the decline in demand, with housing market prospects also exerting substantial downward pressure on housing loan demand."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Net declines were observed across the four largest euro area economies.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"For both loan categories, the net decrease was more moderate than in the previous quarter (-45% for housing loans and -12% for consumer credit) but, for housing loans, more substantial than expected."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first quarter of 2024, banks expect an increase in housing loan demand for the first time since the first quarter of 2022, but a continued decrease in consumer credit demand."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Banks’ overall credit terms and conditions tightened moderately further for firms and consumer credit but eased for housing loans.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net easing in the housing loan category was not accompanied by a corresponding decrease in lending margins and followed seven quarters of tightening (since the first quarter of 2022).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the fourth quarter of 2023, banks reported a further net increase in the share of rejected applications across all loan segments."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The January 2024 BLS contained a number of ad hoc questions. •
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Euro area banks’ access to funding improved somewhat for money markets, long-term deposits and debt securities, while banks’ access to short-term retail funding and securitisation tightened slightly in the fourth quarter of 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Over the next three months, access to funding across all segments except short-term deposits and securitisation is expected to improve. •"
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks indicated that supervisory or regulatory actions contributed to higher levels of capital as well as liquid and risk-weighted assets, and had a net tightening impact on banks’ credit standards and credit margins across most loan categories in 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,A further tightening impact is expected in 2024. •
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,16,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Perceived credit risks in banks’ loan portfolios had a moderate tightening impact on their credit standards for loans to enterprises and consumer credit in the second half of 2023, while the impact was neutral for housing loans."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,17,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Banks expect similar impacts in the first half of 2024. •
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,18,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Lending conditions for firms tightened moderately further in most economic sectors in the second half of 2023, ranging from almost no net tightening in services to relatively large net tightening in the commercial real estate, construction and residential real estate sectors."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,19,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Demand for loans decreased in net terms in all economic sectors, especially in real estate and construction."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,20,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first half of 2024, banks expect further net tightening in lending conditions, albeit lower in all sectors except for construction and services."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,4,21,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,They also expect 4 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Overview of results
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"a moderate further net decrease in loan demand in several economic sectors, mostly concentrated in real estate and construction. •"
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Banks reported that the decline in excess liquidity in the Eurosystem in the second half of 2023 had only a limited impact on bank lending conditions.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Similar effects are expected in the first half of 2024.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Overview table Latest BLS results for the largest euro area countries (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening of credit standards or an increase in loan demand) Enterprises House purchase Consumer credit Credit standards Demand Credit standards Demand Credit standards Demand Q3 23 Q4 23 Avg Q3 23 Q4 23 Avg Q3 23 Q4 23 Avg Q3 23 Q4 23 Avg Q3 23 Q4 23 Avg Q3 23 Q4 23 Avg Country Euro area 12 4 9 -36 -20 -1 11 2 7 -45 -26 0 16 11 5 -12 -7 0 Germany 10 6 4 -23 -16 5 4 0 4 -32 -7 5 7 4 1 -4 -4 6 Spain 8 0 9 -58 -8 -6 30 0 14 -60 -20 -10 42 25 10 -33 -8 -8 France 17 0 7 -25 -17 -4 10 0 4 -60 -60 2 21 14 -1 -29 -14 -2 Italy 18 0 12 -73 -18 4 0 0 1 -45 -36 9 8 23 4 -23 -15 10 Notes: “Avg” refers to historical averages, which are calculated over the period since the beginning of the survey, excluding the most recent round."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Owing to the different sample sizes across countries, which broadly reflect the differences in the national shares in lending to the euro area non-financial private sector, the size and volatility of the net percentages cannot be directly compared across countries."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Box 1 General notes The BLS is addressed to senior loan officers at a representative sample of euro area banks, representing all euro area countries and reflecting the characteristics of their respective national banking structures."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The main purpose of the BLS is to enhance the Eurosystem’s knowledge of bank lending conditions in the euro area.2 Detailed tables and charts based on the responses provided can be found in Annex 1 for the standard questions and Annex 2 for the ad hoc questions.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In addition, BLS time series data are available on the ECB’s website via the ECB Data Portal."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Detailed explanations on the BLS questionnaire, the aggregation of banks’ replies to national and euro area BLS results, the BLS indicators and information on the BLS series keys are available on the ECB’s website in the BLS user guide."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,A copy of the BLS questionnaire and a glossary of BLS terms can also be found on the ECB's website.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"2 For more detailed information on the bank lending survey, see Köhler-Ulbrich, P., Dimou, M., Ferrante, L. and Parle, C., “Happy anniversary, BLS – 20 years of the euro area bank lending survey”, Economic Bulletin, Issue 7, ECB, 2023, Huennekes, F. and Köhler-Ulbrich, P., “What information does the euro area bank lending survey provide on future loan developments?”,"
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Economic Bulletin, Issue 8, ECB, 2022, and Köhler-Ulbrich, P., Hempell, H. and Scopel, S., “The euro area bank lending survey”, Occasional Paper Series, No 179, ECB."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,5,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,5 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Overview of results
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"2 Loans to enterprises 2.1 Credit standards tightened moderately further Euro area banks moderately tightened their credit standards further for loans or credit lines to enterprises in the fourth quarter of 2023 (net percentage of banks of 4%; see Chart 1 and Overview table).3 The tightening adds to the substantial cumulative tightening since 2022, which has contributed, together with weak demand, to the strong fall in loan growth to firms."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The impact of past tightening will continue to dampen loan growth in the coming quarters, in line with the leading indicator properties of credit standards (about 5-6 quarters ahead of actual loan growth developments), such that actual lending to firms can be expected to remain weak in 2024."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The tightening in the fourth quarter was driven by banks in Germany and several smaller euro area countries, while banks in the other three largest euro area economies reported unchanged credit standards."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentage of banks reporting a tightening moderated compared with the previous quarter (12% in the third quarter of 2023) and was lower than banks had expected (7%).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"It was also below the historical average (9%) for the first time since the first quarter of 2022.4 The net tightening of credit standards was similar for loans to small and mediumsized enterprises (SMEs) and for loans to large firms (net percentages of 5% and 4%, respectively; see Chart 2)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,It was stronger for long-term loans (7%) than for short-term loans (4%).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks’ risk perceptions continued to have a tightening impact, while the impact of banks’ cost of funds and balance sheet situation, competition and risk tolerance was broadly neutral at the euro area level in the fourth quarter of 2023 (see Chart 1 and Table 1)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The weak economic situation and outlook, together with credit risk for firms related to their financial situation, were the main underlying reasons for the 3 Net percentages refer to changes over the previous three months (unless otherwise noted) and are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “tightened considerably” and “tightened somewhat” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “eased somewhat” and “eased considerably”."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentages for responses to questions related to the factors are defined as the difference between the percentage of banks reporting that the given factor contributed to a tightening and the percentage reporting that it contributed to an easing. “
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Cost of funds and balance sheet constraints” are defined as the unweighted average of “banks’ capital and the costs related to banks’ capital position”, “access to market financing” and “liquidity position”; “Risk perception” as the unweighted average of “general economic situation and outlook”, “industry or firm-specific situation and outlook/borrower’s creditworthiness” and “risk on collateral demanded”; Competition as “bank competition”, “non-bank competition” and “competition from market financing”."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Owing to different sample sizes across countries, which broadly reflect the differences in the national shares in lending to the euro area non-financial private sector, the size and volatility of the net percentages cannot be directly compared across countries."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,4 The historical average can be taken as a rough proxy for the long-term equilibrium change in credit standards over the business cycle.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"While it is an imperfect measure, as the euro area went through several exceptional tightening periods since the start of the BLS in 2003, such as the global financial crisis, the sovereign debt crisis and the pandemic, excluding these crisis episodes would still result in a historical average above zero (at 6-7%)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Therefore, small positive net percentages – such as the 4% reported in the current round – provide less conclusive evidence for net tightening than larger changes – such as those reported in the survey rounds between the second quarter of 2022 and the third quarter of 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"For comparison, based on the Federal Reserve System Senior Loan Officer Opinion Survey, which started in 1990, the long-term average of the net percentage tightening of credit standards for loans to firms is also positive (5% since the first quarter of 2003 and 6% since the second quarter of 1990 on average across firm sizes), pointing to a moderate tendency of banks for tightening replies over the long term."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,6,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,6 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to enterprises
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,tightening impact of risk perceptions.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Banks in most of the largest euro area economies reported a tightening impact owing to greater credit risks.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Related to this, some banks mentioned the elevated level of interest rates as an additional tightening factor (included in “other factors”).5 By contrast, while banks had reported a lower risk tolerance in previous quarters, contributing to tighter credit standards, banks did not further revise their risk tolerance in the fourth quarter."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks’ own financial situation regarding their capital and liquidity position, as well as their market financing costs, did not contribute to further tightening, with banks in Italy even reporting a net easing impact of their access to market financing."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"According to the banks surveyed, competition had a neutral impact in net terms on credit standards in the fourth quarter of 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Chart 1 Changes in credit standards applied to the approval of loans or credit lines to enterprises, and contributing factors (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening of credit standards and contributing factors) Banks' risk tolerance Risk perceptions Competition Cost of funds and balance sheet constraints Other factors Credit standards - actual Credit standards - expected 40 60 35 50 30 40 25 20 30 15 20 10 10 5 0 0 -5 -10 -10 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q4 2021 Q1 2022 Q2 2022 Q3 2022 Q4 2022 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2024 Germany Spain France Italy Notes: “Actual” values are changes that have occurred, while “expected” values are changes anticipated by banks."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Net percentages are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “tightened considerably” and “tightened somewhat” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “eased somewhat” and “eased considerably”.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentages for responses to questions related to contributing factors are defined as the difference between the percentage of banks reporting that the given factor contributed to a tightening and the percentage reporting that it contributed to an easing. “
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Cost of funds and balance sheet constraints” is the unweighted average of “banks’ capital and the costs related to banks’ capital position”, “access to market financing” and “liquidity position”; “risk perceptions” is the unweighted average of “general economic situation and outlook”, “industry or firm-specific situation and outlook/borrower’s creditworthiness” and “risk related to the collateral demanded”; “competition” is the unweighted average of “competition from other banks”, “competition from non-banks” and “competition from market financing”."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentages for “other factors” refer to an average of the further factors which were mentioned by banks as having contributed to changes in credit standards.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,5 Banks have the option to mention up to three “other factors” for some questions in the questionnaire.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,These “other factors” can be different items across banks and time.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the respective charts, an unweighted net percentage average of the “other factors” is shown, where the net percentage of an “other factor” series is not considered in the calculation when it is equal to zero or no bank has replied to it."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,7,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,7 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to enterprises
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,8,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Chart 2 Changes in credit standards applied to the approval of loans or credit lines to SMEs and large enterprises, and contributing factors (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening of credit standards and contributing factors) Banks' risk tolerance Risk perceptions Competition Cost of funds and balance sheet constraints Other factors Credit standards - actual Credit standards - expected 40 40 30 30 20 20 10 10 0 0 -10 -10 Q4 2021 Q1 2022 Q2 2022 Q3 2022 Q4 2022 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2024 Q4 2021 Q1 2022 Q2 2022 Q3 2022 Q4 2022 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2024 Loans to SMEs Loans to large enterprises Note: See the notes to Chart 1."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,8,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first quarter of 2024, euro area banks expect further net tightening for loans to firms (net percentage of 9%)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,8,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,This would be in line with the historical average net tightening of credit standards for loans to firms since the start of the BLS in 2003 (see above).6 Banks also expect an increase in the net tightening for loans to SMEs (net percentage of 10%) and for loans to large firms (net percentage of 12%).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,8,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Table 1 Factors contributing to changes in credit standards for loans or credit lines to enterprises (net percentages of banks) Cost of funds and balance sheet constraints Pressure from competition Perception of risk Banks’ risk tolerance Country Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Euro area 3 0 0 0 11 9 4 1 Germany 1 0 0 0 8 3 3 0 Spain 6 0 0 0 8 0 8 0 France 8 0 0 3 11 11 0 0 Italy 0 -3 0 0 21 12 9 0 Note: See the notes to Chart 1.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,8,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"6 For the first quarter of 2024, 10% of the banks expected somewhat tighter credit standards and 1% expected somewhat easier credit standards."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,8,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,No bank expected a considerable tightening or considerable easing.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,8,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,8 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to enterprises
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"2.2 Terms and conditions tightened moderately further Banks’ overall terms and conditions for new loans to enterprises tightened moderately further (net percentage of 4%; see Chart 3 and Table 2).7 The net tightening added to the tightening of past quarters, reflecting the pass-through of ECB policy rate hikes and the adjustment of bank lending policies to higher credit risks."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"For the first time since the fourth quarter of 2022, margins on average loans (defined as the spread over relevant market reference rates) have not widened further in net terms at the euro area level but remained broadly unchanged."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"This development was mainly driven by a narrowing of average loan margins by banks in Italy, mainly due to competition by other banks, whereas banks in the other three largest euro area economies reported a further widening of average loan margins."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"By contrast, margins on riskier loans to firms did widen further at the euro area level."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Some banks also referred to the level of interest rates (within “other factors”) as a tightening factor.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In addition to the pricing of new loans, banks also referred to a tightening impact of “other terms and conditions” via loan covenants, collateral requirements and loan size, showing that banks demand additional protection against potential credit losses in the context of higher borrowing costs and weak economic growth."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Overall, the net tightening was smaller in the fourth quarter of 2023, reflecting the unchanged policy rates in the fourth quarter, while the passthrough of policy to lending rates via the bank lending channel continued."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Banks reported a moderate further net tightening of overall terms and conditions for loans to both SMEs and large firms (net percentage for both at 4%; see Chart 4).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"For both, the net tightening was driven by a widening of margins on riskier loans, slightly tighter collateral requirements and some other terms and conditions, especially tighter loan covenants."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Instead, margins on average loans had a broadly neutral impact on overall terms and conditions for both loans to SMEs and large firms."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,7 Terms and conditions are the actual terms and conditions agreed in the loan contract.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,9,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,9 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to enterprises
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,10,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Chart 3 Changes in terms and conditions on loans or credit lines to enterprises (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening of terms and conditions) Margins on average loans Margins on riskier loans Collateral requirements Other terms and conditions Other factors Overall terms and conditions 70 120 60 100 80 50 60 40 40 30 20 20 0 10 -20 0 -40 -10 -60 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 -20 Q4 2021 Q1 2022 Q2 2022 Q3 2022 Q4 2022 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Germany Spain France Italy Notes: “Margins” are defined as the spread over relevant market reference rates. “
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,10,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Other terms and conditions” is the unweighted average of “non-interest rate charges”, “size of the loan or credit line”, “loan covenants” and “maturity”."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,10,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentages for “other factors” refer to an average of the further factors which were mentioned by banks as having contributed to changes in terms and conditions.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,10,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks’ higher risk perceptions and lower risk tolerance continued to be the main drivers of the net tightening in overall terms and conditions for loans to firms, while competition had an easing impact (see Table 3)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,10,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Risk perceptions, related to the economic outlook and the situation of firms, continued to have the largest tightening impact on terms and conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,10,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The net easing impact of competition was mainly related to competition with other banks, especially in Italy (net percentage of -36%)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,10,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Table 2 Changes in terms and conditions on loans or credit lines to enterprises (net percentages of banks) Overall terms and conditions Banks’ margins on average loans Banks’ margins on riskier loans Country Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Euro area 8 4 3 -1 11 4 Germany 13 10 3 3 10 6 Spain 25 8 25 8 25 8 France 8 8 8 8 17 0 Italy 9 -27 -18 -36 0 -9 Note: See the notes to Chart 3.
