ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,11,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,See the notes to Chart 1.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,11,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"2.3 Rejection rates increased In the fourth quarter of 2023, banks reported a further net increase in the share of rejected applications for loans to firms (net percentage of 12%; see Chart 5)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,11,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net share of rejected loan applications has increased every quarter since the start of the ECB policy rate hikes in July 2022.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,11,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net increase was again larger for SMEs than for large firms (net percentages of 16% – the highest on record since the first quarter of 2022 when the series was introduced – and 9% respectively).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,11,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"This reflects the inherent higher credit risk of smaller firms, which is due, among other things, to lower and delayed availability of financial statements."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,11,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The latest increase adds to the 11 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to enterprises
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,higher cumulative increase in the share of loan rejections for SMEs since 2022.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Compared with the third quarter of 2023, the net increase in the share of rejected loan applications rose again."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Chart 5 Changes in the share of rejected loan applications for enterprises (net percentages of banks reporting an increase) Loans to enterprises, overall Loans to SMEs Loans to large enterprises 20 30 20 15 10 10 0 5 -10 0 -20 -5 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q4 2021 Q1 2022 Q2 2022 Q3 2022 Q4 2022 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Germany Spain France Italy Notes: Share of rejected loan applications relative to the volume of all loan applications in that loan category."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The breakdown by firm sizes was introduced in the first quarter of 2022.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,2.4 Net demand for loans continued to decrease markedly Euro area firms’ net demand for loans continued to decrease markedly in the fourth quarter of 2023 (net percentage of -20%; see Chart 6).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"While the net percentage decrease broadly halved compared with its all-time low in the second quarter of 2023 (-42%), the renewed decline added to the substantial net decreases in loan demand seen over the previous four quarters."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The net decrease was widespread, with net declines in all four of the largest euro area economies."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,It was substantially smaller than in the previous quarter (-36%) and in line with euro area banks’ expectations.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The net decreases in demand for loans to SMEs (-17%) and large firms (-15%) were similar and remained substantial, although smaller than in the third quarter of 2023 (- 34% and -36% respectively; see Chart 7)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In addition, demand for long-term loans (net percentage of -22%; see next paragraph) declined more strongly than demand for short-term loans (net percentage of -11%)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,12,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,12 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to enterprises
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,13,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Chart 6 Changes in demand for loans or credit lines to enterprises, and contributing factors (net percentages of banks reporting an increase in demand, and contributing factors) Fixed investment Inventories and working capital General level of interest rates Other financing needs Use of alternative finance Other factors Demand - actual Demand - expected 60 40 40 0 20 -40 0 -20 -80 -40 -120 -60 -80 -160 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 -100 Q4 2021 Q1 2022 Q2 2022 Q3 2022 Q4 2022 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2024 Germany Spain France Italy Notes: “Actual” values are changes that have occurred, while “expected” values are changes anticipated by banks."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,13,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Net percentages for the questions on demand for loans are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “increased considerably” and “increased somewhat” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “decreased somewhat” and “decreased considerably”.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,13,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentages for responses to questions relating to contributing factors are defined as the difference between the percentage of banks reporting that the given factor contributed to increasing demand and the percentage reporting that it contributed to decreasing demand. “
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,13,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Other financing needs” is the unweighted average of “mergers/acquisitions and corporate restructuring” and “debt refinancing/restructuring and renegotiation”; “use of alternative finance” is the unweighted average of “internal financing”, “loans from other banks”, “loans from non-banks”, “issuance/redemption of debt securities” and “issuance/redemption of equity”."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,13,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentages for the “other factors” refer to an average of the further factors which were mentioned by banks as having contributed to changes in loan demand.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,13,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Chart 7 Changes in demand for loans or credit lines to SMEs and large enterprises, and contributing factors (net percentages of banks reporting an increase in demand, and contributing factors) Other factors Fixed investment Demand - actual Inventories and working capital General level of interest rates Demand - expected Other financing needs Use of alternative finance 60 60 40 40 20 20 0 0 -20 -20 -40 -40 -60 -60 -80 -80 -100 -100 Q4 2021 Q1 2022 Q2 2022 Q3 2022 Q4 2022 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2024 Q4 2021 Q1 2022 Q2 2022 Q3 2022 Q4 2022 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2024 Loans to SMEs Loans to large enterprises Note: See the notes to Chart 6."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,13,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Developments in the factors having an impact on loan demand across firm sizes were added in the first quarter of 2022.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,13,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The higher interest rate environment and declining fixed investment remained the main drivers of the net decrease in loan demand (see Chart 6 and Table 4).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,13,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The 13 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to enterprises
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"decline in loan demand was mainly driven by the general level of interest rates8, reported by banks in all four of the largest euro area economies, and lower fixed investment, consistent with the net decrease in demand for long-term loans."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"By contrast, financing needs for inventories and working capital contributed slightly positively to loan demand."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,This was driven by developments in three of the four largest euro area economies (with the exception being Germany).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Debt refinancing or restructuring also contributed positively to loan demand, while the impact of mergers and acquisitions (M&A) financing was broadly neutral at the euro area level."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"With respect to the four largest euro area economies, a positive impact of M&As on loan demand in France was broadly counterbalanced by a negative impact in Germany."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Alternative sources of financing, such as internal financing and marketbased financing via debt securities and corporate equity, dampened loan demand only slightly in the fourth quarter of 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,This would be in line with a limited negative impact of firms’ cash buffers and market-based debt issuance on firms’ bank borrowing.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"For both SMEs and large firms, the general level of interest rates and firms’ financing needs for fixed investment were the main drivers of reduced loan demand (see Chart 7)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Table 4 Factors contributing to changes in demand for loans or credit lines to enterprises (net percentages of banks) Inventories and working capital Other financing needs General level of interest rates Use of alternative finance Fixed investment Country Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Euro area -28 -20 0 2 -5 2 -37 -31 -1 -3 Germany -26 -23 -3 -3 -10 -3 -39 -19 1 1 Spain -42 0 -8 8 -4 0 -58 -17 -2 0 France -8 -17 17 8 0 8 -17 -42 0 -7 Italy -64 -18 -9 18 -9 -5 -64 -36 -7 -7 Note: See the notes to Chart 6.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first quarter of 2024, banks expect a small net increase in demand for loans to firms, for the first time since the second quarter of 2022 (net percentage of 2%)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The expected net increase is related to banks’ expectations for long-term loan demand, while short-term loan demand is expected to remain unchanged."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"While banks’ expectations for long-term loan demand tend to predict actual developments more accurately than those for short-term loan demand, banks had underestimated the steep net decrease in long-term loan demand in 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"8 5% of the euro area banks referred to a “considerable” dampening impact of the general level of interest rates on loan demand, while 28% of the banks referred to a “somewhat” dampening impact."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The weighted net tightening impact of this factor based on the diffusion index moderated to 18% in the fourth quarter of 2023, from 21% in the third quarter of 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,14,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,14 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to enterprises
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,3 Loans to households for house purchase 3.1 Credit standards tightened somewhat further Euro area banks reported a small further net tightening of credit standards on loans to households for house purchase (net percentage of banks at 2%).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"This tightening of credit standards followed six quarters of substantial cumulative tightening, which has contributed to the drag on loan growth."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Taking the historical leading indicator properties of credit standards for loans for house purchase (about two quarters ahead of actual loan developments), the recent net tightening of credit standards can be expected to continue to put a drag on actual lending dynamics to households well into 2024."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentage declined relative to the third quarter of 2023 (11%) and was broadly in line with what banks had expected at that time (1%; see Chart 8 and Overview table).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,It was also below the historical average (6%) and the lowest net percentage since the start of the hiking cycle.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The slight net tightening was driven by smaller euro area countries, with banks in each of the four largest euro area economies citing net unchanged credit standards."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Chart 8 Changes in credit standards applied to the approval of loans to households for house purchase, and contributing factors (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening of credit standards, and contributing factors) Banks' risk tolerance Risk perceptions Competition Cost of funds and balance sheet constraints Other factors Credit standards - actual Credit standards - expected 40 40 30 30 20 20 10 10 0 0 -10 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 -10 Q4 2021 Q1 2022 Q2 2022 Q3 2022 Q4 2022 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2024 Germany Spain France Italy Notes: See the notes to Chart 1. “"
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Cost of funds and balance sheet constraints” is the unweighted average of “banks’ capital and the costs related to banks’ capital position”, “access to market financing” and “liquidity position”; “Risk perceptions” is the unweighted average of “general economic situation and outlook”, “housing market prospects, including expected house price developments” and “borrower’s creditworthiness”; “competition” is the unweighted average of “competition from other banks” and “competition from nonbanks”."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentages for “other factors” refer to an average of the further factors which were mentioned by banks as having contributed to changes in credit standards.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Banks’ higher risk perceptions were the main factor driving the net tightening of credit standards on housing loans (see Chart 8 and Table 5).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Increased risk perceptions were primarily related to perceptions regarding housing market prospects and the general economic outlook.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,15,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks’ risk tolerance, competition as The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to households for house purchase 15"
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,well as banks’ cost of funds and balance sheet constraints had a broadly neutral impact.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first quarter of 2024, euro area banks expect a pick-up in the net tightening of credit standards on loans to households for house purchase (net percentage of 8%)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Among the four largest euro area economies, the expected net tightening is most pronounced in Germany."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Table 5 Factors contributing to changes in credit standards for loans to households for house purchase (net percentages of banks) Cost of funds and balance sheet constraints Pressure from competition Perception of risk Banks’ risk tolerance Country Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Euro area 1 1 -1 -1 9 3 6 1 Germany 0 2 0 -2 4 -1 0 0 Spain 3 0 0 0 13 0 20 0 France 3 0 0 0 7 0 0 0 Italy 0 0 -5 0 12 3 18 0 Note: See the notes to Chart 8.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"3.2 Terms and conditions eased somewhat Banks reported a moderate easing of their overall terms and conditions for new housing loans in the fourth quarter of 2023 (net percentage of -4%; see Chart 9 and Table 6), after seven quarters of successive, sizeable tightening."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"While overall terms and conditions eased, margins on average loans remained broadly unchanged and margins on riskier loans continued to widen, exerting tightening pressure on terms and conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Amongst the largest euro area economies, margins increased in France and Spain, with banks in those countries also reporting even tighter terms and conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"By contrast, banks in Germany and Italy reported narrower margins on average loans and easier terms and conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"For the euro area net percentage, banks mentioned (in “other terms and conditions”) that loan-to-value ratios tightened somewhat, while other loan size limits eased."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentage in the fourth quarter was lower than in the third quarter (19%) and was the first easing since the first quarter of 2022.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,16,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to households for house purchase 16
