ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"3.4 Net demand for loans decreased strongly The net decrease in demand for housing loans remained substantial in the fourth quarter of 2023 but was lower than earlier in the year (net percentage of -26%, after -45% in the previous quarter; see Chart 11 and Overview table)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The decrease in demand was stronger than anticipated by banks in the previous quarter (net percentage of -11%) and played out across the four largest euro area economies.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Actual net decreases in demand have consistently been greater than previous expectations for the same period since the fourth quarter of 2022.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Chart 11 Changes in demand for loans to households for house purchase, and contributing factors (net percentages of banks reporting an increase in demand, and contributing factors) Housing market prospects Consumer confidence General level of interest rates Other financing needs Use of alternative finance Other factors Demand - actual Demand - expected 40 40 0 0 -40 -40 -80 -120 -80 -160 -120 -200 -240 -160 -280 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 -200 Q4 2021 Q1 2022 Q2 2022 Q3 2022 Q4 2022 Q1 2023 Q2 2023 Q3 2023 Q4 2023 Q1 2024 Germany Spain France Italy Notes: See the notes to Chart 6. “"
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Other financing needs” is the unweighted average of “debt refinancing/restructuring and renegotiation” and “regulatory and fiscal regime of housing markets”; “use of alternative finance” is the unweighted average of “internal finance of house purchase out of savings/down payment”, “loans from other banks” and “other sources of external finance”."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net percentages for the “other factors” refer to an average of the further factors which were mentioned by banks as having contributed to changes in loan demand.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Housing loan demand declined primarily due to high interest rates, as well as weakening housing market prospects and low consumer confidence (see Chart 11 and Table 8)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The general level of interest rates continued to be the main negative contributor to housing loan demand, but the net tightening impact became substantially smaller."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Similarly, consumer confidence and housing market prospects had a smaller, but still sizeable negative impact in the fourth quarter of 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Other financing needs and the use of alternative finance (especially internal financing out of savings) contributed negatively to demand to a much smaller extent.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"These developments played out broadly to a similar extent across the four largest euro area economies, with only German banks citing housing market prospects rather than higher interest rates as the main dampening factor, which may be related to the strong decline in house prices in Germany."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first quarter of 2024, banks expect an increase in housing loan demand (net percentage of banks of 5%), which is the first time a demand increase has been expected since the first quarter of 2022."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,19,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Loans to households for house purchase 19
