ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,21,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,4 Consumer credit and other lending to households 4.1 Credit standards tightened further Banks reported a further net tightening of credit standards on consumer credit and other lending to households (net percentage of 11%; see Chart 12 and Overview table).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,21,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The net tightening in credit standards was lower than in the third quarter of 2023 (16%), but broadly in line with banks’ expectations in that quarter (net percentage of 12%)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,21,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"At the same time, it remained well above the historical average (5%) and added to the tightening accumulated since the start of the hiking cycle."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,21,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Credit standards increased across the four largest euro area economies.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,21,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Increased risk perceptions and banks’ lower risk tolerance mainly contributed to the net tightening of credit standards for consumer credit (see Chart 12 and Table 9).9 This was mostly related to banks’ perceptions of the economic outlook and consumers’ creditworthiness.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,21,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Banks’ cost of funds and balance sheet constraints had a broadly neutral impact.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,21,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first quarter of 2024, euro area banks expect a further net tightening of credit standards for consumer credit and other lending to households (net percentage of 11%), especially in Germany."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,21,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"9 “Cost of funds and balance sheet constraints” are defined as an unweighted average of “banks’ capital and the costs related to banks’ capital position”, “access to market financing” and “liquidity position”; “Risk perceptions” as an unweighted average of “general economic situation and outlook”, “borrower’s creditworthiness” and “collateral demanded”; “Competition” as an unweighted average of “competition from other banks” and “competition from non-banks”."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,21,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Consumer credit and other lending to households 21
