ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,26,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Retail funding” is the unweighted average of “short-term deposits (up to one year)” and “long-term (more than one year) deposits and other retail funding instruments”; “money market” refers to the interbank unsecured money market and is the unweighted average of “very short-term money market (up to 1 week)” and “short-term money market (more than 1 week)”; “wholesale debt securities” is the unweighted average of “short-term debt securities (e.g. certificates of deposit or commercial paper)” and “medium to long term debt securities (incl.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,26,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"covered bonds)”; “securitisation” is the unweighted average of “securitisation of corporate loans”, “securitisation of loans for house purchase” and “ability to transfer credit risk off balance sheet”."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,26,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,26 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Ad hoc questions
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Table 13 Changes in banks’ access to retail and wholesale funding (net percentages of banks reporting a deterioration in access) Retail funding Wholesale debt securities Securitisation Total Short-term Long-term Total Short-term Money markets Mediumto long-term Q3 2023 7 11 2 2 2 -2 6 3 Q4 2023 -1 2 -5 -3 -2 -1 -3 2 Q1 2024 -3 0 -7 -8 -7 -9 -4 3 Note: See the notes to Chart 15.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The last period denotes expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first quarter of 2024, banks expect access to funding to improve further across all segments, except for short-term deposits and securitisation."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks expect the net improvement of their access to money markets, long-term retail funding and debt securities funding to improve further."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Access to short-term retail funding is expected to remain unchanged and access to securitisation is expected to continue to tighten in the first quarter of 2024.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,5.2 Banks increased their capital in response to regulatory and supervisory requirements 11 Euro area banks reported an increase in their capital as well as liquid and riskweighted assets in 2023 in response to new regulatory or supervisory requirements (see Chart 16 and Table 14).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Developments in banks’ capital position were driven more by retained earnings than by capital issuance.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks indicated that regulatory or supervisory measures had a positive impact on banks’ total assets, with a similar impact on liquid assets and risk-weighted assets."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The pressure to increase liquid assets may have resulted from the overall decrease in bank liquidity as well as the renewed attention towards banks’ liquidity levels brought about by the March 2023 market turmoil, which originated in the US and Swiss banking systems."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The increase in risk-weighted assets was also supported by an increase in average and riskier loans induced by regulatory and supervisory requirements.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,This reflects either higher risk weights due to supervisors paying more attention to the recognition of impending credit risks or higher volumes due to the phase-out of previous surcharges.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Furthermore, banks indicated that regulatory or supervisory action had a broadly neutral effect on their funding conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,11 The January 2024 BLS questionnaire included an annual ad hoc question to assess the extent to which new regulatory or supervisory requirements affected banks’ lending policies.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"This is ascertained by assessing the potential impact on banks’ capital, leverage, liquidity position or provisioning and the credit conditions that they apply to loans."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,These new requirements cover regulatory or supervisory action that has been implemented recently or that is expected to be implemented in the near future.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Furthermore, banks were also asked to indicate the effects on their funding conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,16,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Until the January 2020 BLS, this question referred to the changes over the past/next six months."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,27,17,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"As of the January 2021 BLS, it refers to the changes over the past 12 months and over the next 12 months."
