ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,29,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The last period denotes expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,29,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Looking ahead to 2024, euro area banks expect that regulatory or supervisory actions will increase their capital positions and their risk-weighted assets, but they do not expect further pressure to increase their liquid assets."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,29,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The further positive net impact on risk-weighted assets, which is expected to be larger in 2024 than in 2023, is in line with higher perceived credit risks."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,29,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The expected muted impact on liquid assets may reflect that, in an environment of overall decreasing liquidity, banks do not expect regulators and supervisors to increase liquidity requirements."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,29,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"At the same time, the actual net impact of supervisory and regulatory actions on liquid assets has been higher than expected by banks."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,29,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In addition, banks expect a slight net tightening impact of regulatory or supervisory action on funding conditions."
