ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,29,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,29 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Ad hoc questions
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,5.3 Perceived credit risks in banks’ loan portfolios had a tightening impact on credit standards12 Euro area banks reported a moderate net tightening impact of non-performing loan (NPL) ratios and other indicators of credit quality on their credit standards for loans to enterprises and consumer credit in the second half of 2023 (see Chart 18 and Table 16).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The net tightening impact of banks’ perceived credit risks on credit standards for loans to firms in the second half of 2023 (3%) was below the average registered since the first half of 2018, while the net tightening impact on terms and conditions (4%) was broadly in line with this average.13 Banks assessed credit quality risks for firms on average as contained, but there were pockets of deteriorating quality in certain segments, such as commercial real estate or construction (see Section 5.4)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In addition, the net tightening impact of banks’ perceived credit risks on credit standards for consumer credit remained highest across loan categories."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"For housing loans, credit quality had a broadly neutral impact on both credit standards and terms and conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,12 The January 2024 BLS questionnaire included a biannual ad hoc question on the impact of banks’ NPL ratios and other indicators of credit quality on changes in their lending policies.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Furthermore, the question asked banks about the factors through which NPL ratios and other indicators of credit quality contributed to changes in their lending policies."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Until the July 2023 BLS, this question referred only to the impact of banks’ NPL ratios."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks were asked about the impact on loans to enterprises, loans to households for house purchase and on consumer credit and other lending to households over the past six months and over the next six months."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The question was extended to “other indicators of credit quality” in January 2024.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The NPL ratio is defined as the stock of gross NPLs on a bank’s balance sheet as a percentage of the gross carrying amount of loans. “
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Other indicators of credit quality” include, for example, Stage 2 loans (performing loans with a significant of credit risk) and loans in early arrears (loans for which payment is overdue for more than 30 and up to 90 days)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Changes in credit standards and/or terms and conditions can be caused by changes in banks’ credit quality, by changes in regulation or in the bank’s assessment of the credit quality, even if the indicators have remained unchanged."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"13 Compared with the impact on credit standards and terms and conditions from 2014-2017 (net percentages of 17% and 11%), when NPL ratios of euro area banks were considerably higher, the current tightening impact is lower."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"When the question was introduced in the July 2018 BLS, it asked about the impact of banks’ NPL ratio “from 2014-2017”, in addition to the impact over the past and next six months."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,30,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,30 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Ad hoc questions
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,31,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Chart 18 Impact of banks’ NPL ratios and other indicators of credit quality on credit standards and terms and conditions (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact) Enterprises Households for house purchase Consumer credit and other lending 12 12 10 10 8 8 6 6 4 4 2 2 0 0 -2 -2 -4 -4 Q3 2021 - Q4 2021 Q1 2022 - Q2 2022 Q3 2022 - Q4 2022 Q1 2023 - Q2 2023 Q3 2023 - Q4 2023 Q1 2024 - Q2 2024 Q3 2021 - Q4 2021 Q1 2022 - Q2 2022 Q3 2022 - Q4 2022 Q1 2023 - Q2 2023 Q3 2023 - Q4 2023 Q1 2024 - Q2 2024 Credit standards Terms and conditions Notes: Net percentages are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed considerably to tightening” and “contributed somewhat to tightening” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed somewhat to easing” and “contributed considerably to easing”.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,31,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Until the July 2023 BLS, this question referred only to the impact of banks’ NPL ratios."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,31,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The last period denotes expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,31,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Table 16 Impact of banks’ NPL ratios and other indicators of credit quality on credit standards and terms and conditions (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact) Credit standards Terms and conditions Q1 2023 - Q2 2023 Q3 2023 - Q4 2023 Q1 2024 - Q2 2024 Q1 2023 - Q2 2023 Q3 2023 - Q4 2023 Q1 2024 - Q2 2024 Loans to enterprises 6 3 7 6 4 5 Loans to households for house purchase 0 1 -1 1 0 0 Consumer credit and other lending to households 7 7 5 10 3 6 Note: See the notes to Chart 18.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,31,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The last period denotes expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,31,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Higher risk perceptions, lower risk tolerance and higher pressure related to supervisory or regulatory requirements remained the main factors behind banks reporting a tightening impact of credit quality on their lending conditions in the second half of 2023 (see Chart 19 and Table 17)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,31,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,This reflects increased refinancing and repayment risks and a more prudent attitude towards credit risks in the context of higher lending rates and weak economic growth.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,31,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In line with the generally sound state of euro area banks, the impact of credit quality on banks’ lending policies from banks’ capital and liquidity positions, market financing access, and cost of balance sheet clean-up was neutral in the second half of 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,31,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,31 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Ad hoc questions
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,32,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Chart 19 Impact of factors through which NPL ratios and other indicators of credit quality affect banks’ policies on lending to enterprises and households (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact) Q1 2023 - Q2 2023 Q3 2023 - Q4 2023 Q1 2024 - Q2 2024 14 12 10 8 6 4 2 0 -2 Access to market Liquidity position Perception of risk Supervisory or Risk tolerance Costs – balance Costs – capital financing regulatory requirements sheet clean-up position Note: See the notes to Chart 18.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,32,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The last period denotes expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,32,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Table 17 Impact of factors through which NPL ratios and other indicators of credit quality affect banks’ policies on lending to enterprises and households (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact) Q1 2023 – Q2 2023 Q3 2023 – Q4 2023 Q1 2024 – Q2 2024 Costs related to banks’ capital position 3 0 1 Costs related to balance sheet clean-up operations 3 0 2 Supervisory or regulatory requirements 6 4 6 Access to market financing 2 0 -1 Liquidity position 2 0 0 Perception of risk 9 12 4 Banks’ risk tolerance 12 6 5 Note: See the notes to Chart 18.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,32,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The last period denotes expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,32,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"For the first half of 2024, euro area banks expect the credit quality of their loans to firms and consumer credit to have a further moderate tightening impact on their credit standards and a continued broadly neutral impact for housing loans."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,32,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Pressure related to supervisory or regulatory requirements, lower risk tolerance and higher risk perceptions are expected to be the main drivers of credit quality affecting credit standards and terms and conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,32,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks’ credit quality is also expected to have a small tightening impact through costs related to balance sheet clean-up, whereas they expect a broadly neutral impact from their capital position and access to market financing over the next six months."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,32,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,32 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Ad hoc questions
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"5.4 Bank lending conditions tightened further in most economic sectors14 Lending conditions for firms tightened moderately further in most economic sectors in the second half of 2023, ranging from almost no net tightening in services to relatively large net tightening in commercial real estate, construction and residential real estate."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Credit standards and terms and conditions continued to tighten most in the commercial real estate sector (CRE), reflecting higher financing costs, falling house prices and structural changes in the CRE segment in the aftermath of the pandemic (see Chart 20 and Table 18).15 The net tightening of credit standards and terms and conditions also remained elevated in the construction sector and the residential real estate sector (RRE) in the second half of 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Reflecting falling energy prices while the situation in manufacturing remained overall weak (see, for instance, the manufacturing output index in the Purchasing Managers’ Index), banks further tightened their lending conditions in the manufacturing sector, but less than in the previous two periods, especially in the energy-intensive segment."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The tightening of bank lending conditions was lowest in the services sector where it was almost nil, reflecting this sector’s higher resilience compared with the weaker situation in the other economic sectors."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Overall, the further net tightening of credit standards and terms and conditions became smaller in all main economic sectors."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first half of 2024, euro area banks expect a net tightening in credit standards and terms and conditions for loans to firms across all economic sectors."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The net tightening is expected to become smaller than in the second half of 2023, except for credit standards in construction and services."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The net tightening of credit standards in CRE is expected to remain very elevated over the next six months.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"14 The January 2024 survey questionnaire included a biannual ad hoc question to collect information on changes in banks’ credit standards, overall terms and conditions and loan demand across the main economic sectors over the past and next six months."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks were asked to report information covering five sectors: manufacturing (with a breakdown into energy-intensive manufacturing), construction (excluding real estate), services (excluding financial services and real estate), wholesale and retail trade, and real estate (including both real estate construction and real estate services)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"15 See the special feature entitled “Real estate markets in an environment of high financing costs” in the ECB Financial Stability Review, November 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,33,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,33 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Ad hoc questions
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Chart 20 Changes in credit standards and terms and conditions for new loans to enterprises across main economic sectors (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening) Manufacturing Construction Of which: energy-intensive manufacturing Wholesale and retail trade Services Commercial real estate Residential real estate 35 35 30 30 25 25 20 20 15 15 10 10 5 5 0 0 -5 -5 Q3 2021 - Q4 2021 Q1 2022 - Q2 2022 Q3 2022 - Q4 2022 Q1 2023 - Q2 2023 Q3 2023 - Q4 2023 Q1 2024 - Q2 2024 Q3 2021 - Q4 2021 Q1 2022 - Q2 2022 Q3 2022 - Q4 2022 Q1 2023 - Q2 2023 Q3 2023 - Q4 2023 Q1 2024 - Q2 2024 Terms and conditions Credit standards Notes: The net percentages refer to the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “tightened considerably” and “tightened somewhat” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “eased somewhat” and “eased considerably”.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The last period denotes expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks reported a net decrease in demand for loans or credit lines in all main economic sectors, which remained especially pronounced in real estate and construction (see Chart 21 and Table 18)."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The strong decline in loan demand in the CRE and RRE sectors reflects higher financing costs, lower collateral values and structural changes in the CRE segment, which dampen loan demand."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Rising lending rates and higher construction costs also dampened loan demand in the construction sector in the second half of 2023.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The net decrease in loan demand was still substantial but more moderate in manufacturing, services and wholesale and retail trade."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"In the first half of 2024, euro area banks expect a moderate further net decrease in loan demand in several economic sectors, mostly concentrated in real estate and construction."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Loan demand is expected to decrease more moderately in the wholesale and retail sector and in RRE, while the net decrease is expected to remain somewhat more pronounced in the construction sector and CRE."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Banks expect broadly unchanged loan demand in manufacturing, while they expect a moderate loan demand increase in the services sector."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"These expectations would overall be in line with the expected gradual recovery in euro area economic activity from the first quarter of 2024 onwards, while some pockets of vulnerabilities are expected to remain.16 16 See the Eurosystem Macroeconomic Projections, December 2023."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,34,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,34 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Ad hoc questions
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,35,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Chart 21 Changes in demand for loans or credit lines to enterprises across main economic sectors (net percentages of banks reporting an increase) Manufacturing Construction Of which: energy-intensive manufacturing Wholesale and retail trade Services Commercial real estate Residential real estate 20 10 0 -10 -20 -30 -40 -50 Q3 2021 - Q4 2021 Q1 2022 - Q2 2022 Q3 2022 - Q4 2022 Q1 2023 - Q2 2023 Q3 2023 - Q4 2023 Q1 2024 - Q2 2024 Notes: The net percentages refer to the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “increased considerably” and “increased somewhat” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “decreased somewhat” and “decreased considerably”.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,35,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The last period denotes expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,35,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Table 18 Changes in credit standards, terms and conditions and demand for new loans to enterprises across main economic sectors (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening/increase) Credit standards Terms and conditions Loan demand Q1 23 - Q2 23 Q3 23 - Q4 23 Q1 24 - Q2 24 Q1 23 - Q2 23 Q3 23 - Q4 23 Q1 24 - Q2 24 Q1 23 - Q2 23 Q3 23 - Q4 23 Q1 24 - Q2 24 Manufacturing 10 8 6 14 6 2 -17 -17 -1 Of which: energyintensive manufacturing 20 15 9 19 8 6 -22 -12 -1 Construction 18 17 20 18 13 12 -26 -24 -11 Services 8 1 4 11 4 0 -17 -7 4 Wholesale and retail trade 18 10 6 18 8 2 -15 -10 -4 Commercial real estate 30 30 28 26 26 15 -42 -39 -11 Residential real estate 19 13 12 26 17 10 -41 -34 -5 Note: See the notes to Charts 20 and 21."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,35,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The last period denotes expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,35,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,35 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Ad hoc questions
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,5.5 Decrease in excess liquidity had a limited impact 17 Banks reported only a limited impact of the decline in excess liquidity held with the Eurosystem in the second half of 2023 on bank lending conditions.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The decline in excess liquidity had a small net tightening impact on credit standards and a moderate net tightening impact on terms and conditions.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,A moderate net percentage of banks also reported a negative impact on loan volumes (see Chart 22 and Table 19).
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The negative contribution of declining excess liquidity was reported as having been similar in both short-term and long-term lending.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Looking to the first half of 2024, banks anticipate a continuation of the effects as reported in the past half year."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Changes in excess liquidity are expected to continue to exert some tightening pressure on credit standards as well as terms and conditions.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The effect on credit standards is expected to slightly increase, while the effect on terms and conditions is expected to moderate slightly."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"The effects on lending volumes are expected to remain negative, at contained levels."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Chart 22 Impact of changes in banks’ excess liquidity with the Eurosystem on bank lending (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact or an increase) Q3 2023 - Q4 2023 Q1 2024 - Q2 2024 6 4 2 0 -2 -4 -6 Credit standards Terms and conditions Lending volumes Lending volumes – shortLending volumes – longterm loans term loans Notes: The net percentages refer to the difference between the percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact or a decrease and the percentages of banks reporting an easing impact or an increase.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"Short-term loans are loans with an original maturity of one year or less, and long-term loans are loans that have an original maturity of more than one year, including onand off-balance sheet credit lines."
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,The last period denotes expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,17 The January 2024 survey questionnaire included an ad hoc question to collect information on the impact of changes in banks' excess liquidity held with the Eurosystem on bank lending over the past six months and over the next six months.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Banks’ excess liquidity with the Eurosystem are the reserves that banks hold in the ECB’s current account or deposit facility.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,They do not include the minimum reserve requirement.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,Changes in banks’ excess liquidity can occur as a result of changes in banks’ liquidity holdings within the ECB’s current account or deposit facility and/or as a result of a change in minimum reserve requirements.
ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,36,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,36 The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023 – Ad hoc questions
