ecb.blssurvey2023q4~6d56dfebf7.en.pdf,39,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Fourth quarter of 2023,European Central Bank,D:20240123092349+01'00',D:20240123092121+01'00',,"PDF ISSN 1830-5989, QB-BA-23-004-EN-N HTML ISSN 1830-5989, QB-BA-23-004-EN-Q"
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,1,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey Second quarter of 2025 July 2025
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,2,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Contents 1 Overview of results 3 Box 1 General notes 6 2 Loans to enterprises 7 2.1 Credit standards remained broadly unchanged 7 2.2 Terms and conditions eased further 9 2.3 Rejection rates increased slightly 11 2.4 Demand for loans increased slightly 12 3 Loans to households for house purchase 15 3.1 Small tightening of credit standards 15 3.2 Terms and conditions remained unchanged 16 3.3 Rejection rates remained broadly unchanged 18 3.4 Demand for loans increased substantially 19 4 Consumer credit and other lending to households 21 4.1 Pronounced tightening of credit standards 21 4.2 Terms and conditions tightened further 22 4.3 Rejection rates increased markedly 24 4.4 Demand for consumer credit increased slightly 24 5 Ad hoc questions 27 5.1 Banks reported an improvement in access to funding 27 5.2 Perceived risks to credit quality had a tightening impact on credit standards 28 5.3 Heterogeneous developments in credit standards and loan demand across main economic sectors 31 5.4 Easing impact of better climate performance on firms’ credit standards but uncertainty regarding future climate regulation seen as an obstacle to loan demand 35 The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Contents 1
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,3,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,5.5 Bank lending conditions eased for buildings with high energy performance and tightened for buildings with low energy performance 39 5.6 Changes in excess liquidity had a neutral impact on bank lending conditions 44 Annexes 46 The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Contents 2
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"1 Overview of results In the July 2025 bank lending survey (BLS), euro area banks reported that credit standards for loans or credit lines to euro area firms remained broadly unchanged in the second quarter of 2025 (net percentage of banks of -1%; see Overview table).1 Perceived risks related to the economic outlook continued to contribute to a tightening of credit standards, whereas competition had an easing impact."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Euro area banks mostly reported no specific additional tightening impact on their credit standards from geopolitical uncertainty and trade tensions, although they intensified their monitoring of the most exposed sectors and firms."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Among the four largest euro area countries, banks in Germany reported a net tightening of credit standards for firms, banks in Italy reported a net easing and banks in Spain and France reported unchanged credit standards."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The net percentage of credit standards for firms was lower than banks had expected in the previous survey (net tightening of 5%) and follows a small net tightening in credit standards in the first quarter (3%).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For the third quarter of 2025, banks expect unchanged credit standards for firms (0%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Banks reported a small net tightening of credit standards for housing loans and a more pronounced net tightening for consumer credit (net percentages of 2% and 11% respectively).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Changes in risk perceptions and the risk tolerance of banks were the main drivers of the tightening for both household loan segments.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Across the largest euro area countries, credit standards for housing loans remained unchanged in Spain, France and Italy, while banks in Germany reported a net tightening."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Credit standards for consumer credit tightened in all of the four largest euro area countries.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The overall net tightening was less than anticipated by euro area banks in the first quarter for housing loans and larger for consumer credit (7% in both segments).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For the third quarter of 2025, banks expect credit standards to ease slightly for housing loans (-3%) and to tighten further for consumer credit (4%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Firms’ demand for loans increased slightly, in net terms, in the second quarter of 2025 (net percentage of 2%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"It remained weak overall, supported by declining lending rates but dampened by global uncertainty and trade tensions."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,This followed a small net decrease in loan demand in the previous quarter (-3%).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Firms’ loan demand was supported in the second quarter by declining lending rates, while the impact of fixed investment and inventories and working capital was neutral."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Several banks referred to a dampening impact on loan demand from global uncertainty and the related trade tensions.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,16,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks in Germany and Italy reported a net increase of firms’ loan demand, while banks in France reported a net decrease and banks in Spain zero change in loan demand in net terms."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,17,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For the third quarter of 2025, banks expect a net increase in loan demand (7%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,18,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,1 The results reported in the July 2025 survey relate to changes observed during the second quarter of 2025 and expectations for the third quarter of 2025.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,19,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The survey was conducted between 13 June and 1 July 2025.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,20,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"A total of 155 banks were surveyed in this round, with a response rate of 100%."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,21,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"In addition to results for the euro area as a whole, this report contains results for the four largest euro area countries in terms of GDP (i.e. Germany, Spain, France and Italy)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,4,22,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Overview of results 3
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks reported a further substantial net increase in demand for housing loans, while consumer credit demand increased only slightly (net percentages of 37% and 2%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Declining interest rates, improved housing market prospects and, to a lesser extent, consumer confidence, were the primary drivers of the continued increase in housing loan demand."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The net increase was observed across a wide range of euro area countries – it was only slightly lower than in the previous quarter (41%) and was above banks’ expectations (20%).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Consumer credit demand was also supported by declining interest rates, together with “other factors”, offsetting the negative contributions from lower consumer confidence and spending on durable goods."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The net increase in demand for consumer credit was lower than in the previous quarter (10%) and banks’ expectations (6%).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For the third quarter of 2025, banks expect demand for housing loans to increase further (21%), while remaining broadly unchanged for consumer credit (1%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Euro area banks’ overall credit terms and conditions eased for loans to firms, remained unchanged for housing loans and tightened for consumer credit."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For firms, lower lending rates and narrower margins on average loans contributed to an easing of terms and conditions, while margins on riskier loans led to tighter lending conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For housing loans, lending rates and margins, including margins on riskier loans, contributed to an easing of terms and conditions, although less than in the previous quarter."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For consumer credit, margins on both riskier and average loans contributed the most to the tightened terms and conditions, followed by lending rates and collateral requirements."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks reported a small net increase in the share of rejected loan applications for firms, a more pronounced net increase for consumer credit and a broadly unchanged share for housing loans."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The July 2025 BLS contained the following ad hoc questions: • Euro area banks’ access to retail funding improved slightly in the second quarter of 2025, driven by short-term retail funding, eased moderately for money markets and debt securities, and remained broadly unchanged for securitisations."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Access to debt securities eased more strongly for medium to long-term securities.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Over the next three months, banks expect access to these funding sources to remain broadly unchanged. •"
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Euro area banks reported a net tightening impact of NPL ratios and other credit quality indicators on their credit standards across loan categories, and a net tightening impact on terms and conditions for loans to firms and consumer credit."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks expect these trends to continue in the third quarter for firm loans and consumer credit, driven mostly by pressures related to supervisory or regulatory requirements. •"
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,16,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Changes in credit standards and loan demand were heterogeneous across the main economic sectors in the first half of 2025.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,5,17,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Credit standards tightened in commercial real estate (CRE), manufacturing, wholesale and retail trade and, to a lesser extent, construction, while they eased slightly across most services (excluding financial services and real estate) and in residential real estate The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Overview of results 4"
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks reported a net decrease in demand for loans in the construction, manufacturing, and wholesale and retail sectors, consistent with the overall weakness in loan demand and the dampening impact of global uncertainty, as well as in CRE."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"They reported net increases in demand in RRE and in transport, accommodation and food services."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For the second half of 2025, banks expect either broadly unchanged or easier credit standards in most main economic sectors and overall small changes in loan demand."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The exception is RRE, for which banks expect a further moderate increase. •"
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Banks continue to consider firms’ climate performance in their lending policies.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,They reported an easing impact on credit standards and terms and conditions for green firms and firms in transition and a tightening impact for high-emitting firms over the past 12 months.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Both physical risk and firms’ transition risk had a moderate net tightening impact on banks’ lending policies, while climate-related fiscal support continued to have an easing impact."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks also reported a net increase in demand for loans to green firms and firms in transition owing to climate change, while uncertainty over future climate regulation was perceived as an obstacle."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Banks expect an overall similar impact over the next 12 months. •
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Based on a new question on the impact of climate change on housing loans, banks reported an easing impact of climate change on credit standards for buildings with high energy performance and a tightening impact for buildings with low energy performance over the past 12 months."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,They expect a broadly corresponding impact over the next 12 months.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"As the easing impact for new buildings mostly offsets the tightening impact for old buildings, the net impact of energy performance was low."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The physical risk of real estate was, however, an important driver of further net tightening in lending conditions overall, and an even higher net percentage of banks indicated that it will be a driver over the next year."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Banks also reported a positive impact on loan demand for buildings with high and medium energy performance but a negative impact for those with low energy performance.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Investment in energy performance was the key factor for climate-related loan demand, supported by preferential lending rates for increasing sustainability, whereas uncertainty about future climate regulation was reported as a dampening factor for loan demand. •"
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Banks reported that changes in excess liquidity held with the Eurosystem in the first half of 2025 had a neutral impact on bank lending conditions.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,16,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Banks expect similar impacts during the second half of 2025.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,6,17,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Overview of results 5
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,7,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Overview table Latest BLS results for the largest euro area countries (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening of credit standards or an increase in loan demand) Enterprises House purchase Consumer credit Credit standards Demand Credit standards Demand Credit standards Demand Q1 Q2 Q1 Q2 Q1 Q2 Q1 Q2 Q1 Q2 Q1 Q2 Country 25 25 Avg 25 25 Avg 25 25 Avg 25 25 Avg 25 25 Avg 25 25 Avg Euro area 3 -1 9 -3 2 -1 -7 2 6 41 37 2 3 11 5 10 2 0 Germany 3 3 4 3 23 5 -7 11 4 59 52 7 0 11 2 11 18 7 Spain 0 0 9 8 0 -6 0 0 13 60 40 -9 0 8 11 33 0 -6 France 0 0 6 -9 -27 -5 -25 0 2 25 25 3 8 17 0 0 -25 -2 Italy 0 -9 11 0 18 3 9 0 1 45 9 9 8 23 5 31 0 10 Notes: “Avg” refers to historical averages, which are calculated over the period since the beginning of the survey, excluding the most recent round."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,7,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Owing to the different sample sizes across countries, which broadly reflect the differences in the national shares in lending to the euro area non-financial private sector, the size and volatility of the net percentages cannot be directly compared across countries."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,7,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Box 1 General notes The BLS is addressed to senior loan officers at a representative sample of euro area banks, representing all euro area countries and reflecting the characteristics of their respective national banking structures."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,7,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The main purpose of the BLS is to enhance the Eurosystem’s knowledge of bank lending conditions in the euro area.2 Detailed tables and charts based on the responses provided can be found in Annex 1 for the standard questions and Annex 2 for the ad hoc questions.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,7,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"In addition, BLS time series data are available on the ECB’s website through the ECB Data Portal – see also the notes to charts throughout this report."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,7,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Detailed explanations on the BLS questionnaire, the aggregation of banks’ replies to national and euro area BLS results, the BLS indicators and information on the BLS series keys are available on the ECB’s website in the BLS user guide."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,7,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,A copy of the BLS questionnaire with the standard questions and a glossary of BLS terms can also be found on the ECB BLS webpage.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,7,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"2 For more detailed information on the bank lending survey, see Köhler-Ulbrich, P., Dimou, M., Ferrante, L. and Parle, C., “Happy anniversary, BLS – 20 years of the euro area bank lending survey”, Economic Bulletin, Issue 7, ECB, 2023, also Huennekes, F. and Köhler-Ulbrich, P., “What information does the euro area bank lending survey provide on future loan developments?”,"
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,7,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Economic Bulletin, Issue 8, ECB, 2022."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,7,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Overview of results 6
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,2 Loans to enterprises 2.1 Credit standards remained broadly unchanged Credit standards for loans or credit lines to euro area firms remained broadly unchanged in the second quarter of 2025 (net percentage of banks of -1%; see Chart 1 and Overview table).3 The net percentage follows a small net tightening in credit standards for loans to firms in the first quarter of 2025 (3%) and was smaller than banks had expected in the previous survey round (net tightening of 5%).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Across the four largest euro area countries, banks in Germany reported a net tightening of credit standards on loans to firms, banks in Italy reported a net easing and banks in Spain and France reported unchanged credit standards."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The net percentage was broadly equal to the net percentage in the second quarter of 2021 and was lower than the historical average (9%).4 Credit standards remained broadly unchanged for loans to small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), while they eased for loans to large firms (net percentages of 1% and -3% respectively; see Chart 2)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Across maturities, banks reported broadly unchanged credit standards for both short-term loans (1%) and long-term loans (0%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Perceived risks related to the general economic and the industry and firm-specific outlook contributed to tighter credit standards, as reported by banks in all four large euro area countries (see Chart 1 and Table 1)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The tightening impact from perceived credit risks is also consistent with the net tightening impact of non-performing loan (NPL) ratios and other indicators of asset quality on banks’ credit standards for loans to enterprises (see Section 5.2).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Based on a dedicated open-ended question which was included in this survey round, euro area banks mostly reported no specific additional tightening impact on their credit standards related to geopolitical uncertainty and trade tensions over the past three months."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"However, they reported intensified monitoring of the credit risks of their potentially most affected corporate customers (especially exporters with high levels of US exposure)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Competition from banks and, to a lesser extent, from non-banks, had a net easing impact on credit standards for loans to firms."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Among the four large euro area countries, the easing impact of competition was concentrated in Italy."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Euro area banks’ risk tolerance and banks’ cost of funds and balance sheet situations had a broadly neutral impact on credit standards for loans to firms.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,3 Credit standards are the internal guidelines or loan approval criteria of a bank.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Net percentages for credit standards refer to changes over the previous three months and are defined as the difference between the percentages of banks reporting a tightening and the percentages of banks reporting an easing.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Owing to different sample sizes across countries, which broadly reflect the differences in the national shares in lending to the euro area non-financial private sector, the size and volatility of the net percentages cannot be directly compared across countries."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"4 Historical averages over different time periods can be taken as rough proxies for the long-term equilibrium change in credit standards, terms and conditions and loan demand over the business cycle."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For credit standards, although the figure is imperfect given that the euro area has been through several exceptional tightening periods since the BLS was launched in 2003 (such as, in particular, the global financial crisis and the sovereign debt crisis), the historical net percentage average tightening of credit standards for loans to firms since 2003 is 9%."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,16,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The average net tightening of credit standards since 2014 is 3%.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,8,17,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Loans to enterprises 7
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,9,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Chart 1 Changes in credit standards applied to the approval of loans or credit lines to enterprises, and contributing factors (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening of credit standards and contributing factors) Notes: “Credit standards - actual” are changes that have occurred, while “Credit standards - expected” are changes anticipated by banks."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,9,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Net percentages are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “tightened considerably” and “tightened somewhat” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “eased somewhat” and “eased considerably”. “
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,9,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Cost of funds and balance sheet constraints” is the simple average of “banks’ capital and the costs related to banks’ capital position”, “access to market financing” and “liquidity position”; “Risk perceptions” is the simple average of “general economic situation and outlook”, “industry or firm-specific situation and outlook/borrower’s creditworthiness” and “risk related to the collateral demanded”. “"
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,9,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Competition” is the simple average of “competition from other banks”, “competition from non-banks” and “competition from market financing”."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,9,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The net percentages for “Other factors” refer to an average of the further factors which were mentioned by banks as having contributed to changes in credit standards.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,9,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal links: euro area and largest four euro area countries.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,9,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Chart 2 Changes in credit standards applied to the approval of loans or credit lines to SMEs and large enterprises, and contributing factors (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening of credit standards and contributing factors) Notes: See the notes to Chart 1."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,9,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal links: loans to SMEs and loans to large enterprises.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,9,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For the third quarter of 2025, euro area banks expect credit standards for loans to firms to remain unchanged (net percentage of 0%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,9,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Banks expect unchanged credit The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Loans to enterprises 8
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"standards for loans to SMEs and large firms (both at 0%), and broadly unchanged credit standards for short-term loans (-1%) and long-term loans (1%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Table 1 Factors contributing to changes in credit standards for loans or credit lines to enterprises (net percentages of banks) Cost of funds and balance sheet Pressure from constraints competition Perception of risk Banks’ risk tolerance Country Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Euro area 0 -1 -1 -2 7 4 1 1 Germany -2 0 0 0 9 4 0 0 Spain 0 -3 0 0 0 3 0 0 France 0 0 0 0 6 3 0 0 Italy 0 0 0 -3 6 3 0 0 Note: See the notes to Chart 1.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"2.2 Terms and conditions eased further Overall terms and conditions for new loans to enterprises eased further (net percentage of -10%; see Chart 3 and Table 2).5 According to the banks, the net easing was mainly driven by lower lending rates and narrower margins on average loans."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"This is in line with the further decline in bank lending rates for firms in April and May, based on MFI interest rate statistics."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Banks also reported that margins on riskier loans tightened slightly.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks in Spain, France and Italy reported a net easing of terms and conditions on loans to firms."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"In the case of Spain and Italy this was driven mostly by declining lending rates, whereas banks in France reported a net easing of non-interest rate charges and loan size (within “other terms and conditions”)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"By contrast, banks in Germany reported a slight net tightening of their terms and conditions for loans to firms, driven mainly by lending rates and loan margins, and to a lesser extent by loan size, maturity and loan covenants."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Some banks reported that global uncertainty and US tariff policy have led to actual changes in their lending conditions over the past three months, indicating tighter lending conditions via interest rates, loan sizes and maturity."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Across segments, euro area banks reported a net easing in overall terms and conditions for loans to large firms and SMEs (net percentages of -12% and -7% respectively; see Chart 4)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"In both cases, lending rates and narrower margins on average loans were the main drivers of the net easing, while wider margins on riskier loans had a limited net tightening impact."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,5 Terms and conditions are the actual terms and conditions agreed in the loan contract.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The historical net percentage average of overall terms and conditions for loans to firms since 2015, when the series was introduced, is 0%."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,10,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Loans to enterprises 9
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Chart 3 Changes in terms and conditions on loans or credit lines to enterprises (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening of terms and conditions) Notes: “Overall terms and conditions” are the actual terms and conditions agreed in the loan contract. “
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Lending rates” was introduced in April 2024. “
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Margins” are defined as the spread over relevant market reference rates. “
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Other terms and conditions” is the simple average of “non-interest rate charges”, “size of the loan or credit line”, “loan covenants” and “maturity”."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The net percentages for “Other components” refer to an average of the further terms and conditions components which were mentioned by banks as having contributed to changes in overall terms and conditions.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal links: euro area and largest four euro area countries.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Table 2 Changes in terms and conditions on loans or credit lines to enterprises (net percentages of banks) Overall terms and Banks’ margins on Banks’ margins on riskier conditions Banks’ lending rates average loans loans Country Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Euro area -10 -10 -8 -11 -9 -7 0 2 Germany 10 3 7 3 3 6 3 3 Spain -25 -25 -25 -25 -25 -17 0 0 France -18 -9 0 0 -9 0 -9 0 Italy -45 -55 -55 -73 -36 -45 0 -9 Note: See the notes to Chart 3.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The main factor contributing to the net easing of terms and conditions for loans to euro area firms was competition, and especially competition from other banks (see Table 3)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Competition with non-banks also had a small easing impact.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks also reported a small net easing impact of their cost of funds and balance sheet situation, on account of access to market financing, banks’ liquidity position and capital costs."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"This is in line with the moderation in bank funding costs in the second quarter, as the temporary increase in bank bond spreads in April in the context of the US tariff announcements was fully compensated by a repricing of the risk-free curve."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,11,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Perceived risks contributed to a small net tightening of credit conditions, while banks’ risk tolerance had a broadly neutral impact."
