ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,12,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"2.3 Rejection rates increased slightly Banks reported a small net increase in the share of rejected loan applications for firms (net percentage of 2%, see Chart 5)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,12,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The net increase in the share of loan rejections was driven by loan rejections to SMEs (net percentage of 5%), while the share remained broadly unchanged for loans to large firms (1%), pointing to either somewhat higher credit risks on average for SMEs or changes in banks’ lending The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Loans to enterprises 11"
