ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,13,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"2.4 Demand for loans increased slightly Euro area banks reported a slight net increase in loan demand from firms in the second quarter of 2025, remaining weak overall (net percentage of 2%; see Chart 6).6 This followed a small net decrease in loan demand in the previous quarter (-3%) and was broadly in line with what banks had expected in the previous quarter (4%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,13,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The continued weakness in loan demand to euro area firms is consistent with the subdued developments in actual lending to firms in April and May, according to monetary statistics."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,13,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks in Germany and Italy reported that demand for loans to firms increased in the second quarter in net terms, while banks in Spain referred to unchanged demand and banks in France reported a net decrease."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,13,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Across loan segments, banks reported a net increase in loan demand from SMEs and broadly unchanged loan demand for large firms (net percentages of 4% and 0% respectively, see Chart 7)."
