ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"3.4 Demand for loans increased substantially Banks reported a further substantial net increase in demand for housing loans (net percentage of 37%, see Chart 11 and Overview table).10 A net increase was reported in Germany (52%), Spain (40%), France (25%) and Italy (9%, in line with its historical average)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The net increase was somewhat lower than in the previous quarter (41%) but constitutes the fifth consecutive quarter reporting strong expansion in net terms.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"It is also the second quarterly reading that is above banks’ expectations (20%), especially in Germany and Spain and, to a lesser extent, in Italy."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The reported net increase in demand appears to be at odds with the moderation of the lending flows in this type of credit seen in April and May 2025.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"This suggests that either the volumes of new business for each bank registering an increase in loan demand is still contained, or the slight tightening of credit standards reported by banks during the second quarter (see Section 3.1) may already be in play, affecting actual lending volumes."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Chart 11 Changes in demand for loans to households for house purchase, and contributing factors (net percentages of banks reporting an increase in demand, and contributing factors) Notes: “Demand - actual” represents changes that have occurred, while “Demand - expected” represents changes anticipated by banks."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Net percentages for the questions on demand for loans are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “increased considerably” and “increased somewhat” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “decreased somewhat” and “decreased considerably”. “
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Other financing needs” is the simple average of “debt refinancing/restructuring and renegotiation” and “regulatory and fiscal regime of housing markets”. “
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Use of alternative finance” is the simple average of “internal finance of house purchase out of savings/down payment”, “loans from other banks” and “other sources of external finance”."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The net percentages for “Other factors” refer to an average of the further factors which were mentioned by banks as having contributed to changes in loan demand.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal links: euro area and largest four euro area countries.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Declining interest rates, improved housing market prospects and, to a lesser extent, consumer confidence, were the primary drivers of the continued increase in housing loan demand (see Chart 11 and Table 8)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"These factors were relevant across the 10 “Other financing needs” is the simple average of “debt refinancing/restructuring and renegotiation” and “regulatory and fiscal regime of housing markets”; “Use of alternative finance” is the simple average of “internal financing out of savings/down payment”, “loans from other banks” and “other sources of external finance”."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The historical net percentage average of demand for housing loans since 2003 is 2%.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The average net increase of housing loan demand since 2014 is 8%.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,20,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Loans to households for house purchase 19
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,21,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"four largest countries, except for housing market prospects in Italy which had a neutral impact on demand."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,21,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The reported contribution of declining interest rates was lower than in the previous quarter across all the largest countries in the euro area.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,21,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"In the third quarter of 2025, banks expect housing loan demand to continue growing, albeit more moderately (net percentage of 21%)."
