ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,22,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The average net tightening of credit standards since 2014 is 3%.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,22,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Consumer credit and other lending to households 21
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Lower risk tolerance and higher risk perceptions were the main drivers of the net tightening of credit standards for consumer credit (see Chart 12 and Table 9).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,These two factors were mentioned by banks in all four largest euro area countries.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Lower risk tolerance was reported more frequently than in the previous quarter across all countries.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The higher impact of risk perceptions related to concerns about borrowers’ creditworthiness (8%) but also the general economic outlook (4%) and the collateral demanded (3%).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Competition and banks’ balance sheet situation had a broadly neutral impact.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"In the third quarter of 2025, euro area banks expect credit standards for consumer credit and other lending to households to tighten further (net percentage of 4%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Across the four largest euro area economies, banks in Germany and France expect a net tightening, while banks in Spain and Italy expect unchanged credit standards."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Table 9 Factors contributing to changes in credit standards for consumer credit and other lending to households (net percentages of banks) Cost of funds and balance sheet Pressure from constraints competition Perception of risk Banks’ risk tolerance Country Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Euro area 1 0 -1 0 3 5 1 6 Germany -1 0 0 0 6 5 4 7 Spain 0 0 0 0 0 3 0 8 France 3 0 -4 0 6 8 0 8 Italy 0 0 0 0 3 8 0 8 Note: See the notes to Chart 12.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,4.2 Terms and conditions tightened further Banks’ overall terms and conditions applied when granting consumer credit and other lending to households tightened further in the second quarter of 2025 (net percentage of 8%; see Chart 13 and Table 10).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The net percentage of euro area banks reporting a tightening was in line with the previous quarter and above the historical average since 2015 (2%).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Higher margins on both riskier and average loans contributed the most to the tightened terms and conditions, followed by lending rates and collateral requirements."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Loan size and maturity had a marginal additional tightening effect.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Across the four largest euro area economies, overall terms and conditions tightened in Germany, France and Italy and remained unchanged in Spain."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks in Germany and Italy reported an easing contribution from lower lending rates, while banks in France reported an increased contribution."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Lending margins widened in Germany and France (for both average and riskier loans) and in Spain (for riskier loans), while they narrowed in Italy for average loans."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Tightened collateral requirements were reported in France and Italy.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,23,16,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Consumer credit and other lending to households 22
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,24,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Higher perceived risks and a lower risk tolerance of banks contributed the most to the net tightening of banks’ overall terms and conditions (see Table 11).
