ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Table 15 Impact of factors through which NPL ratios and other credit quality indicators affect banks’ policies on lending to enterprises and households (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact) Q1 2025 Q2 2025 Q3 2025 Costs related to banks’ capital positions 5 2 2 Costs related to balance sheet clean-up operations 0 2 1 Supervisory or regulatory requirements 7 5 7 Access to market financing 1 0 0 Liquidity position 1 0 0 Perception of risk 8 8 5 Banks’ risk tolerance 6 5 3 Notes: See the notes to Chart 18.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The last period shows expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Looking ahead, euro area banks expect a further tightening impact of credit quality on their lending conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For loans to firms, both credit standards and terms and conditions are expected to be affected."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For loans to households, terms and conditions are expected to be affected but the impact on credit standards is expected to be neutral for housing loans."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The factors that had a tightening impact in the current quarter are expected to continue to exert tightening pressure in the near future, with supervisory or regulatory requirements leading the impacts."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"5.3 Heterogeneous developments in credit standards and loan demand across main economic sectors15 Credit standards tightened in CRE, manufacturing, wholesale and retail trade and, to a lesser extent, in construction in the first half of 2025, while easing slightly in various segments of services (excluding financial services and real estate) and in RRE (see Chart 19 and Table 16)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The net tightening of credit standards in CRE and in wholesale and retail trade was lower than in previous quarters, while the net tightening in the manufacturing sector was higher, potentially reflecting perceived risks in the context of global uncertainty, despite some upward movement of the euro area manufacturing Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"15 The July 2025 survey questionnaire included a biannual ad hoc question aimed at collecting information on changes in banks’ credit standards, overall terms and conditions and loan demand across the main economic sectors over the past/next six months."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks were asked to report information covering five sectors: manufacturing (with a breakdown for energy-intensive manufacturing); construction (excluding real estate); services (excluding financial services and real estate, broken down into transport, accommodation and food as well as into other services); wholesale and retail trade; and real estate (including both real estate construction and real estate services). “"
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Other services” include mainly administration, scientific, technical, information and social services."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Since the January 2023 BLS and the January 2025 BLS respectively, breakdowns have been included for the manufacturing sector and the services sector."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,32,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 31
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,33,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Chart 19 Changes in credit standards for new loans to enterprises across main economic sectors (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening) Notes: Net percentages refer to the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “tightened considerably” and “tightened somewhat” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “eased somewhat” and “eased considerably”.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,33,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The last period shows expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,33,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal link: changes in credit standards for new loans to enterprises across main economic sectors.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,33,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Terms and conditions followed a similar pattern to credit standards in the first half of 2025, tightening slightly for manufacturing and easing slightly for services (excluding financial services and real estate), except for a further limited net tightening in the CRE sector (see Chart 20 and Table 16)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,33,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Compared with credit standards, the net tightening of credit terms and conditions was mostly more limited, while the net easing was overall similar across the respective sectors."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,33,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Overall, the heterogeneity across the main economic sectors as regards the net tightening and easing of credit standards in the first half of 2025 is consistent with the small net tightening of overall credit standards for loans to firms in the first quarter of 2025 and broadly unchanged credit standards in the second quarter."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,33,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For the second half of 2025, euro area banks expect either broadly unchanged or easier credit standards for most main economic sectors."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,33,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Exceptions are the energyintensive manufacturing sector and CRE sector, for which banks expect a small further net tightening in the second half of 2025."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,33,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For credit terms and conditions, banks expect a net easing for most main economic sectors in second half of 2025, except for CRE and energy-intensive manufacturing, for which banks expect terms and conditions to remain broadly unchanged."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,33,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 32
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Chart 20 Changes in terms and conditions for new loans to enterprises across main economic sectors (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening) Notes: Net percentages refer to the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “tightened considerably” and “tightened somewhat” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “eased somewhat” and “eased considerably”.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The last period shows expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal link: changes in terms and conditions for new loans to enterprises across main economic sectors.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks reported a net decrease in demand for loans in the construction, manufacturing, CRE and wholesale and retail sectors in the first half of 2025, and a net increase in RRE and some services sectors (excluding financial services and real estate) (see Chart 21 and Table 16)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The net decrease in loan demand was also pronounced in energy-intensive manufacturing.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,These developments are broadly consistent with the overall weakness in loan demand and the dampening impact of global uncertainty.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Loan demand increased in RRE together with a limited net increase in the transport, accommodation and food sector."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Loan demand in the rest of the services sectors (excluding financial services and real estate) remained broadly unchanged.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For the second half of 2025, euro area banks expect small changes overall in loan demand across the main economic sectors, except for RRE where demand is expected to increase moderately."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Loan demand is expected by banks to remain broadly unchanged in the second half of 2025 in manufacturing (including in energyintensive manufacturing), construction and CRE."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"A small net increase is expected for both segments of the services sector, while a limited net decrease is expected for wholesale and retail trade."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,34,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 33
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,35,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Chart 21 Changes in demand for loans or credit lines to enterprises across main economic sectors (net percentages of banks reporting an increase) Notes: Net percentages refer to the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “increased considerably” and “increased somewhat” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “decreased somewhat” and “decreased considerably”.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,35,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The last period shows expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,35,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal link: changes in demand for loans or credit lines to enterprises across main economic sectors.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,35,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Table 16 Changes in credit standards, terms and conditions and demand for new loans to enterprises across main economic sectors (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening/increase) Credit standards Terms and conditions Loan demand Q3– Q4 Q1– Q2 Q3– Q4 Q3– Q4 Q1– Q2 Q3– Q4 Q3– Q4 Q1– Q2 Q3– Q4 2024 2025 2025 2024 2025 2025 2024 2025 2025 Manufacturing 4 7 -2 0 2 -4 -1 -14 -1 Of which: energyintensive manufacturing 13 5 3 2 2 -1 -2 -12 -1 Construction 14 2 -3 7 1 -3 -7 -15 1 Services (excluding financial services and real estate) 3 -2 0 -2 -2 -4 2 -2 3 Of which: transport, accommodation and food 5 -1 -3 -2 -3 -3 -1 3 3 Of which: other services -1 0 0 -3 -2 -4 3 -1 2 Wholesale and retail trade 16 5 1 1 3 -3 0 -6 -3 Commercial real estate 16 9 2 8 5 -1 -12 -8 1 Residential real estate 7 -3 -2 0 -3 -3 1 8 9 Notes: See the notes to Charts 19, 20 and 21."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,35,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The last period shows expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,35,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 34
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"5.4 Easing impact of better climate performance on firms’ credit standards but uncertainty regarding future climate regulation seen as an obstacle to loan demand16 Banks continue to take the climate performance of firms into account in their lending policy, reporting an easing impact on credit standards and terms and conditions for firms with better climate performance and a tightening impact for high carbon emitting firms which have not yet started their transition (see Chart 22 and Table 17).17 Over the past 12 months, euro area banks have reported a substantial net easing impact of climate risks and measures to cope with climate change on their credit standards and terms and conditions (net percentages of -20% and -31% respectively) for loans to green firms, i.e. firms that do not contribute or contribute little to climate change, which was somewhat smaller than expected by banks one year ago (-29% and -37%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"A net easing impact was also reported by banks for loans to firms in transition, i.e. firms which have implemented a climate plan to reduce their carbon emissions (net percentages of -13% and -20% respectively), and was somewhat more than expected one year ago, especially for terms and conditions (-12% and -14%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"By contrast, climate risks had a substantial net tightening impact for loans to high-emitting firms (net percentages of 35% and 22% respectively), although this is smaller than expected by banks one year ago (50% and 40%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,16 The July 2025 survey questionnaire included an annual ad hoc question aimed at gauging the impact of climate change on bank lending to firms.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"This impact relates to climate-related risks and measures to cope with climate change implemented by governments, monetary policy as well as supervisory and regulatory authorities."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,It can also relate to banks’ further measures related to climate change.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Firms may be affected by climate change in their firm-specific situation and outlook, with respect to their creditworthiness and the value of their assets."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Climate risks can be grouped into two categories: transition risk and physical risk.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Transition risk refers to the risk related to an institution’s financial loss that can result, directly or indirectly, from the process of adjustment towards a lower-carbon and more environmentally sustainable economy."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Physical risk refers to the risk related to the financial impact from banks’ exposure to a changing climate, including more frequent extreme weather events and gradual changes in climate, as well as of environmental degradation, which can affect the value of collateral and borrower repayment capacity."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,17 “Green firms” are defined as firms that contribute little or nothing to climate change; “firms in transition” are firms that contribute to climate change but are making relevant progress in the transition; “brown/high-emitting firms” are firms that contribute significantly to climate change and have not yet started the transition or made little progress.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,36,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 35
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,37,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Chart 22 Impact of climate change on banks’ credit standards and terms and conditions for loans to firms (net percentages of banks; over the past 12 months and the next 12 months) Notes: For definitions of “green firms”, “firms in transition” and “brown firms”, see the footnote at the beginning of this section."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,37,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Net percentages are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed considerably to tightening” and “contributed somewhat to tightening” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed somewhat to easing” and “contributed considerably to easing”.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,37,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The striped bars denote expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,37,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal link: impact of climate change on banks’ credit standards and terms and conditions for loans to firms.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,37,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Table 17 Impact of climate change on banks’ credit standards, terms and conditions and demand for loans to firms (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact or an increase) Credit standards Terms and conditions Demand Q3 2023 - Q3 2024 - Q3 2025 - Q3 2023 - Q3 2024 - Q3 2025 - Q3 2023 - Q3 2024 - Q3 2025 - Q2 2024 Q2 2025 Q2 2026 Q2 2024 Q2 2025 Q2 2026 Q2 2024 Q2 2025 Q2 2026 Green firms -25 -20 -22 -31 -31 -28 24 22 21 Firms in transition -10 -13 -17 -14 -20 -17 24 24 24 Brown firms 44 35 33 31 22 26 -3 -3 -6 Notes: See the notes to Chart 22."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,37,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The last period shows expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,37,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Both physical risk and firms’ transition risk had a moderate net tightening impact on banks’ lending policy for euro area firms over the past 12 months, while climaterelated fiscal support continued to have an easing impact (net percentages of 11%, 8% and -3% respectively; see Chart 23 and Table 18).18 Banks’ capital costs related to their exposure to climate risk had only a small tightening impact on banks’ lending policy (net percentage of 2%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,37,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The net easing impact of climate-related fiscal support on banks’ lending conditions was in line with their expectations one year ago.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,37,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,18 Banks’ lending policy covers changes in both credit standards and terms and conditions.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,37,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 36
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,38,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Chart 23 Impact of climate-related factors on banks’ lending policy to firms (net percentages of banks; over the past 12 months and the next 12 months) Notes: Net percentages are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed considerably to tightening” and “contributed somewhat to tightening” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed somewhat to easing” and “contributed considerably to easing”.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,38,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The striped bars denote expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,38,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal link: impact of climate-related factors on banks' lending policy to firms.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,38,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Table 18 Impact of climate-related factors on banks’ lending policy and loan demand for firms (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact or an increase) Q3 2023 - Q3 2024 - Q3 2025 - Q2 2024 Q2 2025 Q2 2026 Impact on banks’ lending policy through: Costs related to banks’ capital position -1 2 1 Industry or firm-specific situation and outlook (transition risk) 14 8 1 Physical risk 18 11 9 Climate-related fiscal support -2 -3 -7 Impact on loan demand through: Climate-related fixed investment and corporate restructuring 22 17 25 Prevailing climate-related regulation - 2 1 Uncertainty about future climate-related regulation - -11 -13 Bank lending rates for green projects or technologies - 21 22 Use of alternative financing sources other than fiscal support 10 1 2 Climate-related fiscal support 0 2 8 Notes: See the notes to Charts 23 and 24.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,38,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The factors related to climate-related regulation and bank lending rates were introduced in this survey round. “
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,38,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Use of alternative financing other than fiscal support” includes, among other things, the issuance of green corporate bonds."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,38,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The last period shows expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,38,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Over the next 12 months, euro area banks expect a broadly similar impact from climate change on their lending conditions, driven by a further net tightening impact from physical risk and a broadly unchanged impact from transition risk, while the relevance of climate-related fiscal support to ease lending conditions is expected to increase (net percentages of 9%, 1% and -7% respectively)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,38,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Banks’ capital costs related to their climate exposure are expected to have a broadly neutral impact (1%).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,38,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 37
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Euro area banks reported a net increase in demand for loans to firms in transition and green firms owing to climate change over the past 12 months (net percentages of 24% and 22% respectively), and a net decrease in loan demand for high-emitting firms (net percentage of -3%; see Chart 24 and Table 17)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Fixed investment and corporate restructuring in combination with bank lending rates for green projects or technologies were reported by banks as the main drivers of climate-related loan demand (net percentages of 17% and 21% respectively; see Chart 25 and Table 18).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Climate-related fiscal support had also a small supportive impact over the past 12 months.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"By contrast, the uncertainty about future climate regulation was perceived by banks as an important obstacle to loan demand (net percentage of -11%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"According to the banks, the impact of the current climate regulation on loan demand was on average slightly positive over the past 12 months (2%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Over the next 12 months, loan demand is expected to increase owing to climate risks for firms in transition and green firms (net percentages of 24% and 21% respectively), while it is expected to decrease for high-emitting firms (net percentage of -6%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Fixed investment and corporate restructuring, bank lending rates for green projects or technologies, and, to a small extent, climate-related fiscal support are expected to have a positive impact on climate-related loan demand, while the uncertainty regarding future climate regulation is expected to remain an important obstacle over the next 12 months."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Chart 24 Impact of climate change on demand for loans to firms (net percentages of banks; over the past 12 months and the next 12 months) Notes: For definitions of “green firms”, “firms in transition” and “brown firms”, see footnote at the beginning of this section."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Net percentages are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed considerably to an increase” and “contributed somewhat to an increase” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed somewhat to a decrease” and “contributed considerably to a decrease”.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The striped bars denote expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal link: impact of climate change on demand for loans to firms, and climate-related contributing factors."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,39,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 38
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Chart 25 Impact of climate-related factors on demand for loans to firms (net percentages of banks; over the past 12 months and the next 12 months) Notes: For definitions of “green firms”, “firms in transition” and “brown firms”, see footnote at the beginning of this section."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Net percentages are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed considerably to an increase” and “contributed somewhat to an increase” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed somewhat to a decrease” and “contributed considerably to a decrease”.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The factors related to climate-related regulation and bank lending rates were introduced in this survey round. “
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Use of alternative financing” excludes fiscal support and includes, among others, the issuance of green corporate bonds."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The striped bars denote expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal link: impact of climate change on demand for loans to firms, and climate-related contributing factors."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"5.5 Bank lending conditions eased for buildings with high energy performance and tightened for buildings with low energy performance19 Banks reported an easing impact of climate change on credit standards for buildings with high energy performance, while tighter credit standards were applied to buildings with low energy performance (net percentages of -14% and 25% respectively; see Chart 26 and Table 19)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,A new ad hoc question on the impact of climate change on loans to households for house purchase shows that the energy performance of buildings is a relevant criterion for banks when granting housing loans.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Similar to the impact on credit standards, banks also reported a net easing impact on their credit terms and conditions for housing loans for buildings with high 19 The July 2025 survey questionnaire included a new annual ad hoc question aimed at gauging the impact of climate change on bank lending to households for house purchase."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Housing loans to households may be affected by climate change, for instance in respect of the energy efficiency of the real estate or physical risks, often related to the geographical location of the real estate."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Buildings with “High energy performance” are defined as new buildings or equivalent to new in their energy performance (Energy Performance Certificate A-B).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Buildings with “Medium energy performance” are defined buildings with reasonably good energy performance, i.e., modern buildings/existing buildings with major energetic modernisation other than equivalent to new (Energy Performance Certificate C-E)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Buildings with “Low energy performance” are defined as buildings with poor energy performance, i.e., old buildings without major energetic modernisation (Energy Performance Certificate F-G)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"If no Energy Performance Certificate (EPC) is available, the bank may use the age of the building and whether a major energetic modernisation has taken place or the actual energy consumption of the building (i.e., the amount of energy consumed, typically measured in kWh) as a proxy."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,14,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Existing buildings built since 2000 or buildings with a major energetic modernisation other than equivalent to new may be classified as EPC C-E. Buildings built before 2000 without a major energetic modernisation may be classified as EPC F-G. See also the EU Energy Performance of Buildings Directive (EU/2024/1275).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,15,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"For further explanation, see the footnotes in Section 5.4 on the impact of climate change on bank lending to firms."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,40,16,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 39
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,41,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"energy performance and, to a small extent, for buildings with medium energy performance over the past 12 months, whereas climate change had a tightening impact for buildings with low energy performance (net percentages of -30%, -2% and 22% respectively)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,41,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Chart 26 Impact of climate change on banks’ credit standards and terms and conditions for loans to households for house purchase (net percentages of banks; over the past 12 months and the next 12 months) Notes: For definitions of “high energy performance”, “medium energy performance” and “low energy performance”, see the footnote at the beginning of this section."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,41,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Net percentages are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed considerably to tightening” and “contributed somewhat to tightening” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed somewhat to easing” and “contributed considerably to easing”.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,41,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The striped bars denote expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,41,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal link: impact of climate change on banks’ credit standards and terms and conditions for loans to households for house purchase.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,41,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Table 19 Impact of climate change on banks’ credit standards, terms and conditions and demand for loans to households for house purchase (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact or an increase) Credit standards Terms and conditions Demand Q3 2024 - Q3 2025 - Q3 2024 - Q3 2025 - Q3 2024 - Q3 2025 - Q2 2025 Q2 2026 Q2 2025 Q2 2026 Q2 2025 Q2 2026 High energy performance -14 -20 -30 -25 24 28 Medium energy performance 1 -2 -2 1 7 8 Low energy performance 25 28 22 24 -12 -19 Notes: See the notes to Chart 26."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,41,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The last period shows expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,41,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Physical risk of real estate was, in net terms, the main climate-related factor for housing loans with a tightening impact on banks’ lending policy (net percentage of 11%; see Chart 27 and Table 20).20 Euro area banks also reported a small net tightening impact of the transition risk stemming from the energy performance of buildings and a small net easing impact of banks’ capital costs due to their climate 20 Banks’ lending policy covers changes in both credit standards and terms and conditions."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,41,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 40
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,42,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"exposure and of climate-related fiscal support (net percentages of 2%, -3% and -2% respectively)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,42,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The low net impact of energy performance of buildings could be partly related to the shares of housing loans granted over the past 12 months for new buildings (easing impact for buildings with high energy performance) and the renovation of old buildings (tightening impact for buildings with low energy performance).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,42,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Over the next 12 months, euro area banks expect a continued easing impact on their credit standards and terms and conditions for housing loans for buildings with high energy performance and a tightening impact for buildings with low energy performance (net percentages of -20% and 28% respectively for credit standards; net percentages of -25% and 24% respectively for terms and conditions)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,42,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Physical risk of real estate is expected to remain the main climate-related tightening factor in net terms, with a limited net easing impact from the energy performance of the buildings, banks’ capital costs due to their climate exposure and climate-related fiscal support."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,42,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Chart 27 Impact of climate-related factors on banks’ lending policy to households for house purchase (net percentages of banks; over the past 12 months and the next 12 months) Notes: Net percentages are defined as the difference between the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed considerably to tightening” and “contributed somewhat to tightening” and the sum of the percentages of banks responding “contributed somewhat to easing” and “contributed considerably to easing”.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,42,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The striped bars denote expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,42,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal link: impact of climate-related factors on banks' lending policy to households for house purchase.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,42,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 41
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Table 20 Impact of climate-related factors on banks’ lending policy and loan demand for households for house purchase (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact or an increase) Q3 2024 - Q2 2025 Q3 2025 - Q2 2026 Impact on banks’ lending policy through: Costs related to banks’ capital position -3 -3 Energy performance of buildings (transition risk) 2 -5 Physical risk of the real estate 11 16 Climate-related fiscal support -2 -2 Impact on loan demand through: Investment in the energy performance of buildings 36 39 Investment in the reduction of physical risk 2 7 Prevailing climate-related regulation -1 1 Uncertainty about future climate-related regulation -9 -2 Bank lending rates for increasing the sustainability of real estate 24 20 Climate-related fiscal support 6 7 Notes: See the notes to Charts 26 and 27.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The last period shows expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Euro area banks reported a positive impact of climate change on housing loan demand for buildings with high and medium energy performance and a negative impact for buildings with low energy performance over the past 12 months (net percentages of 24%, 7% and -12% respectively; see Chart 28 and Table 19)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"While 75% of the stock of buildings in the EU have a poor energy performance according to the European Commission21 and would require energy modernisation, the evidence from the banks points rather to increasing housing loan demand for new buildings with high energy standards and to the modernisation of existing buildings with medium energy performance."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"By contrast, the evidence from the banks points to subdued demand for housing loans for buildings with low energy performance."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Investment in the energy performance of buildings was the key factor for climaterelated loan demand over the past 12 months (net percentage of 36%; see Chart 29 and Table 20).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Preferential lending rates for increasing the sustainability of real estate and, to a smaller extent, fiscal support also had a positive impact on climaterelated housing loan demand (net percentages of 24% and 6% respectively)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Investment in the reduction of physical risk had only a small positive impact (net percentage of 2%), pointing to a focus of households on the energy performance of buildings."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"By contrast, uncertainty about future climate regulation was reported by banks to have a dampening impact on housing loan demand."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Over the next 12 months, climate-related housing loan demand is expected, in net terms, to increase for buildings with high and medium energy performance (net percentages of 28% and 8% respectively)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"By contrast, a net decrease in climaterelated housing loan demand is expected for buildings with low energy performance (net percentage of -19%)."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,While investment in energy performance and lending rates 21 See information from the European Commission in the context of the Energy Performance of Buildings Directive.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,43,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025 – Ad hoc questions 42
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,44,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"for increasing the sustainability of real estate are expected to remain the main drivers, flanked by climate-related fiscal support, banks expect demand to be mainly for new or relatively modern buildings while they are sceptical about the modernisation progress for old buildings with low energy performance over the next 12 months."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,44,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Chart 28 Impact of climate change on demand for loans to households for house purchase (net percentages of banks; over the past 12 months and the next 12 months) Notes: For definitions of “high energy performance”, “medium energy performance” and “low energy performance”, see footnote at the beginning of this section."
