ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,0,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,5.6 Changes in excess liquidity had a neutral impact on bank lending conditions22 Banks indicated that changes in excess liquidity held with the Eurosystem in the first half of 2025 had a neutral impact on bank lending conditions (see Chart 30 and Table 21).
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,1,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Changes in excess liquidity held at the bank level also did not materially impact lending volumes.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,2,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"As regards the change in aggregate excess liquidity held by other euro area banks, banks reported no impact on lending volumes, on their terms and conditions, and on credit standards."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,3,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,During the second half of 2025 banks expect broadly neutral impacts from changes in excess liquidity.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,4,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Both changes in excess liquidity at the bank level and changes in the excess liquidity held by other banks are expected to have a broadly neutral impact on bank lending conditions.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,5,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Chart 30 Impact of changes in banks’ excess liquidity with the Eurosystem on bank lending (net percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact or an increase) Notes: Net percentages refer to the difference between the percentages of banks reporting a tightening impact or a decrease and the percentages of banks reporting an easing impact or an increase.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,6,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Results until the second quarter of 2024 refer to banks’ excess liquidity held with the Eurosystem without specifying whether it refers to one bank’s excess liquidity or to the aggregate excess liquidity of other euro area banks.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,7,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The last period shows expectations indicated by banks in the current round.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,8,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,The full set of data underlying this chart can be downloaded via the following ECB Data Portal link: impact of changes in banks’ excess liquidity with the Eurosystem on bank lending.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,9,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,22 The July 2025 survey questionnaire included an ad hoc question aimed at collecting information on the impact of changes in banks’ excess liquidity held with the Eurosystem on bank lending over the past/next six months.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,10,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Banks’ excess liquidity with the Eurosystem is the reserves that banks hold in the ECB’s current account or deposit facility, excluding the minimum reserve requirement."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,11,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,Changes in banks’ excess liquidity can occur as a result of changes in banks’ liquidity holdings within the ECB’s current account or deposit facility or a change in minimum reserve requirements.
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,12,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Until the first half of 2024, this ad hoc question referred to excess liquidity held with the Eurosystem without specifying whether it referred to an individual bank’s excess liquidity or to the aggregate excess liquidity of other euro area banks."
ecb.blssurvey2025q2~caacd3537b.en.pdf,45,13,The euro area bank lending survey - Second quarter of 2025,European Central Bank,D:20250721173135+02'00',D:20250721173026+02'00',,"Since the second half of 2024, the reported impacts distinguish between these two aspects."
