raised their deposit rates by less - a pattern we interpret as banks leveraging a more valuable deposit franchise to fund longer-duration assets. Although euro-area banks as a whole avoided widespread runs, several institutions nonetheless carried substantial mark-to-market losses, suggesting latent fragilities.",The frailty of this situation was starkly illustrated in early 2023 by the turmoil among US regional banks - exemplified by the failure of Silicon Valley Bank (SVB) - where substantial unrealised losses combined with depositor flight triggered insolvency.
