raised their deposit rates by less - a pattern we interpret as banks leveraging a more valuable deposit franchise to fund longer-duration assets. Although euro-area banks as a whole avoided widespread runs, several institutions nonetheless carried substantial mark-to-market losses, suggesting latent fragilities.","Understanding this latent vulnerability, masked by favourable flow dynamics and accounting conventions, is crucial for a comprehensive assessment of bank resilience, representing a core motivation for this paper’s focus on economic valuation."
