raised their deposit rates by less - a pattern we interpret as banks leveraging a more valuable deposit franchise to fund longer-duration assets. Although euro-area banks as a whole avoided widespread runs, several institutions nonetheless carried substantial mark-to-market losses, suggesting latent fragilities.",The y-axis is calculated as the ratio of economic net worth to the volume of uninsured deposits.24 We do this exercise using our estimates for both September 2023 13a and March 2023 13b.
