ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,0,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.",A Data appendix This section provides a detailed description of the datasets used for our analysis.
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,1,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.",Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE) is a European firm-level survey launched in 2009.
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,2,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","The survey was conducted twice a year until 2023: once by the ECB, covering euro area countries (around 11,000 firms), and once in cooperation with the European Commission (EC), covering all EU and some EU neighboring countries (around 16,000 firms)."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,3,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.",These survey rounds covered Q2-Q3 and Q4 and Q1 of the next year.
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,4,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","Following a pilot phase that lasted between June 2023 and December 2023, the survey frequency is increased to quarterly as of 2024 Q1."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,5,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","Two new survey rounds have been introduced to cover Q1 and Q3 for a reduced sample of almost 6,000 euro area firms."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,6,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","The samples of the earlier round covering Q2-Q3 and Q4-Q1 have been split so that around 40 % of the sample replies on a quarterly basis (covering Q2 and Q4, respectively) while the other 60 % of the sample keeps replying on a bi-annual basis (covering Q2-Q3 and Q4-Q1)."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,7,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","The sample comprises non-financial firms across manufacturing, construction, trade, and services sectors."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,8,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.",More than 90 % of surveyed firms are small and medium enterprises (SMEs).
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,9,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.",Firms in the sample are randomly selected from the Dun & Bradstreet business register.
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,10,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","The sample is stratified by country, enterprise size class, and economic activity and the sample size is chosen to ensure a satisfactory representation across activities and size classes."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,11,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","The data does not have a panel structure by design, although some firms participate in multiple rounds."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,12,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","The survey contains mainly qualitative information on various firm characteristics (for example, employment, sector, autonomy, turnover, age, and ownership) and on each firm’s assessment of recent developments associated with its economic situation and its financing, including the firm’s financing needs and its access to finance."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,13,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","Since the 2023 Q2-Q3 round, firms in the SAFE were also asked about their quantitative expectations regarding the percentage change over the next 12 months in their average selling prices, non-labour costs, wages and number of employees."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,27,14,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","In addition, as of 2023 Q2, the survey also asks firms about their inflation expectations for the euro area on the 1-, 3- and 5-year horizons. ECB Working Paper Series No 3097 26"
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,28,0,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","ECB Governing Council meetings and monetary policy shocks Our analysis considers the period Q2 2023 - Q1 2024, period for which the SAFE survey provides information on firms’ selling price expectations."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,28,1,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","In addition, the aim is to cover the recent monetary policy tightening cycle, therefore, we focus on the following ECB Governing Council meetings: • Governing Council meeting of 16 March 2023."
ecb.wp3097~5b10420116.en.pdf,28,2,The cost channel of monetary policy: evidence from euro area firm-level survey data,"Ugo Albertazzi, Annalisa Ferrando, Sofia Gori, Judit Rariga",D:20250813135630+02'00',D:20160704163336+02'00',"This paper explores empirically the cost channel of monetary policy transmission during the recent period of monetary policy tightening in the euro area. We combine unique data on firms’ selling price expectation from the Survey on the access to finance of enterprises (SAFE), information on firms’ borrowing from the euro area-wide credit register (AnaCredit) and ECB monetary policy surprises. Firms revise upwards their one-year-ahead selling price expectations following monetary announcements in a tightening cycle and this effect increases in firms’ working capital exposure. The paper provides supportive evidence on the existence of a cost channel of monetary policy, adding to our understanding of monetary policy transmission to firms in the euro area.","The three key interest rates are increased by 50 basis points, with the main refinancing operation (MRO), marginal lending facility (MLF) and the deposit facility (DFR) rates reaching 3.50%, 3.75% and 3.00%, respectively."
