funds, thereby boosting demand and compressing risk premia.","Substituting the optimal portfolio allocations from Equation 12 and Equation 13 into the market clearing condition in Equation 15, we obtain:  ¯δ Pt −Rf t   PtS −ACBXCB t −AL t ψ −AL t ¯X  Et[Rt+1 −Rf t ] = AM t γMV art(Rt+1), (16) where the equilibrium condition incorporates both bond managers’ and long-term investors’ demand functions."
