funds, thereby boosting demand and compressing risk premia.","At the end of 2021, the ECB began signaling a shift to tighter monetary policy, first by scaling back its asset purchases and, from July 2022 on, by raising the deposit rate (with which it steers the monetary policy stance) from -0.5% to 4.0%."
