ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,12,14,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.","After observing the policy action, a, the private sector optimally updates its expectations regarding X1 t as follows: E(X1|sp, a) = E(X1|sp) + k2(a −E(a|sp)), (6) where k2 ≡ αV AR(X1|sp) V AR(X1|sp)α2+α2σ2 ξ,g+σ2ε,a. Note that this gain is negative because α < 0 as the private sector understands policy actions to be countercyclical."
ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,12,15,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.","A negative gain k2 implies that if the magnitude of the policy action, a, exceeds the private sector’s ex-ante expectations E(a|sp), the private sector will revise its expectations about the the appendix."
