ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,23,0,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.","Measuring Uncertainty In our analysis, we use both marketand survey-based measures of uncertainty."
ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,23,1,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.","Our marketbased measure of uncertainty is the Nikkei 225 Volatility Index, which reflects the volatility of the Nikkei 225 stock market index."
