ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,47,1,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.",The dates “Order” are the dates in which the Prime Minister orders the fiscal stimulus packages or supplementary budgets.
ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,47,2,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.",The dates “Size” are those in which the draft of the package is finalized.
ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,47,3,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.","Lastly, the dates “Ratify” are those in which the budget supporting the fiscal stimulus package is officially ratified by the Cabinet."
ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,47,4,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.",Some packages using reserve funds do not require additional budget approval and therefore do not have a Ratify date. ECB Working Paper Series No 3110 46
ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,48,0,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.",Uncertainty Measures This section presents the two measures of uncertainty used in the main text.
ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,48,1,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.","Subsection B.2.1 shows the Nikkei volatility index, a stock market measure of uncertainty, while Subsection B.2.2 presents households’ and firms’ survey measures of disagreement."
ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,48,2,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.","The Nikkei Volatility Index In Section 5, we use the Nikkei 225 Volatility Index (Nikkei VI) – a daily measure of the expected volatility of stock prices – as a proxy for stock markets’ uncertainty."
ecb.wp3110~f44ac33453.en.pdf,48,3,The signaling effects of fiscal announcements,"Leonardo Melosi, Hiroshi Morita, Anna Rogantini Picco, Francesco Zanetti",D:20250910142949+02'00',D:20250826093010Z,"Announcing a large fiscal stimulus may signal the government’s pessimism about the severity of a recession to the private sector, impairing the stabilizing effects of the policy. Using a theoretical model, we show that these signaling effects occur when the stimulus exceeds expectations and are more noticeable during periods of high economic uncertainty. Analysis of a new dataset of daily stock prices and fiscal news in Japan supports these predictions. We introduce a method to identify fiscal news with different degrees of signaling effects and find that such effects weaken or, in extreme cases, even completely undermine the stabilizing impact of the announcements.",This index reflects the stock market’s uncertainty regarding the near-term economic outlook.
